1
00:00:01,307 --> 00:00:04,477
We'll now begin the mothers' game.

2
00:00:04,477 --> 00:00:07,446
Please change into comfortable clothes
and come out.

3
00:00:08,447 --> 00:00:10,116
What do you think we'll be doing?

4
00:00:10,116 --> 00:00:13,152
Maybe the winner gets to choose a date.

5
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,454
What game will we play today?

6
00:00:15,454 --> 00:00:17,857
Last time,
they had a shoe-throwing contest.

7
00:00:17,857 --> 00:00:18,858
Will it be the same?

8
00:00:19,458 --> 00:00:20,593
(They arrive at the game site
full of questions.)

9
00:00:20,593 --> 00:00:22,428
What kind of game could it be?

10
00:00:22,962 --> 00:00:25,131
Isn't that the finish line?

11
00:00:25,131 --> 00:00:27,099
I think we'll be running.

12
00:00:27,099 --> 00:00:29,669
Warm up your legs!
We don't know what we'll do.

13
00:00:29,669 --> 00:00:30,770
Keep those legs moving.

14
00:00:31,437 --> 00:00:32,738
What could it be?

15
00:00:33,539 --> 00:00:36,676
We'll now begin the mothers' game.

16
00:00:37,009 --> 00:00:40,580
The mothers who place first or second
in either group...

17
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:42,381
will earn the right
to a private conversation.

18
00:00:44,183 --> 00:00:46,786
Each winning mother may choose...

19
00:00:46,786 --> 00:00:49,288
one contestant and ask them...

20
00:00:49,288 --> 00:00:51,824
anything she wants to know.

21
00:00:51,824 --> 00:00:53,459
- The moms?
- Yes.

22
00:00:54,594 --> 00:00:55,995
Since they were giving us
that opportunity,

23
00:00:55,995 --> 00:00:59,365
I knew I had to win and take first place.

24
00:01:00,499 --> 00:01:03,236
I was determined
to give it everything I had...

25
00:01:03,236 --> 00:01:05,404
and give Jeong Yoon another chance.

26
00:01:06,038 --> 00:01:07,406
The event is...

27
00:01:08,241 --> 00:01:09,642
the hula-hoop race.

28
00:01:10,877 --> 00:01:12,111
But my back hurts.

29
00:01:12,111 --> 00:01:13,412
It's a hula-hoop race.

30
00:01:13,412 --> 00:01:14,513
A hula-hoop race?

31
00:01:14,513 --> 00:01:16,282
That won't be easy.

32
00:01:16,782 --> 00:01:18,684
We have to race while hula-hooping?

33
00:01:18,684 --> 00:01:20,019
It's been so long since I've done this.

34
00:01:21,721 --> 00:01:23,990
It's hard enough
just to walk with a hula hoop.

35
00:01:25,591 --> 00:01:27,393
Shall we have a practice round?

36
00:01:28,494 --> 00:01:30,997
(Practice time before the real race)

37
00:01:31,831 --> 00:01:34,934
(Giving it her all)

38
00:01:35,301 --> 00:01:36,669
Ma'am.

39
00:01:36,669 --> 00:01:37,803
She's really going for it.

40
00:01:39,171 --> 00:01:42,308
(Hula-hoop race rules,
If the hoop falls to the ground,)

41
00:01:42,308 --> 00:01:44,877
(restart from where it fell.)

42
00:01:46,178 --> 00:01:49,582
(They all practice hard
for their children.)

43
00:01:49,582 --> 00:01:51,117
This isn't easy.

44
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:55,755
There's always at least one person...

45
00:01:56,756 --> 00:01:58,157
who's great with a hula hoop.

46
00:01:58,157 --> 00:02:00,860
(Jeong Yoon's mother,
the hula-hoop master, appears.)

47
00:02:02,161 --> 00:02:03,729
Jeong Yoon's mother is really good.

48
00:02:04,130 --> 00:02:05,932
My back suddenly feels fine.

49
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,534
Anything to get my daughter married.

50
00:02:08,534 --> 00:02:09,936
I felt the same,
but now I'm out of breath.

51
00:02:10,603 --> 00:02:12,838
But anything can happen in the real race.

52
00:02:12,838 --> 00:02:13,940
That's right.

53
00:02:14,574 --> 00:02:17,677
Let's begin the women's mothers' race.

54
00:02:20,947 --> 00:02:22,582
(Game face on)

55
00:02:22,582 --> 00:02:23,816
Ready.

56
00:02:24,917 --> 00:02:27,520
(Go)

57
00:02:29,455 --> 00:02:30,556
My goodness.

58
00:02:31,591 --> 00:02:32,758
She's good.

59
00:02:32,758 --> 00:02:34,594
(Da Hye's mother surges into the lead.)

60
00:02:37,196 --> 00:02:40,199
Da Hye's mother is good. Hurry!

61
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:45,171
(Do Yoon's mother closes in.)

62
00:02:46,806 --> 00:02:48,274
(Jeong Yoon's mother is moving fast too.)

63
00:02:48,274 --> 00:02:49,475
Wait.

64
00:02:49,475 --> 00:02:50,543
Careful.

65
00:02:53,512 --> 00:02:55,314
They're neck-and-neck.

66
00:02:58,751 --> 00:03:02,255
(Which mothers will earn
a private conversation?)

67
00:03:04,457 --> 00:03:05,892
(First place is Choi Jeong Yoon's mother.)

68
00:03:05,892 --> 00:03:07,393
She's fast.

69
00:03:09,362 --> 00:03:11,330
(Second place is Ahn Do Yoon's mother.)

70
00:03:12,265 --> 00:03:13,699
(Third place is Kim Da Hye's mother.)

71
00:03:13,699 --> 00:03:14,534
I knew Jeong Yoon's mother would win.

72
00:03:14,534 --> 00:03:16,035
That was really close.

73
00:03:16,035 --> 00:03:17,436
Da Hye's mother must be disappointed.

74
00:03:17,436 --> 00:03:18,437
Yes, probably.

75
00:03:18,437 --> 00:03:19,705
I did my best.

76
00:03:20,806 --> 00:03:22,742
I'll announce the results
of the women's mothers' race.

77
00:03:22,742 --> 00:03:25,344
First place goes to
Choi Jeong Yoon's mother.

78
00:03:27,246 --> 00:03:30,082
Second place goes to
Ahn Do Yoon's mother.

79
00:03:32,585 --> 00:03:34,420
(Applause)

80
00:03:35,054 --> 00:03:36,556
(The men's mothers begin practicing.)

81
00:03:36,556 --> 00:03:38,291
- It won't spin.
- I can't do this.

82
00:03:38,291 --> 00:03:39,859
I heard...

83
00:03:39,859 --> 00:03:41,594
Ye Chan's mother...

84
00:03:41,594 --> 00:03:43,563
- does belly dancing as a hobby.
- Really?

85
00:03:43,563 --> 00:03:45,031
Then...

86
00:03:45,031 --> 00:03:47,033
Ye Chan's mother is amazing at this.

87
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:49,135
I can do this for over an hour.

88
00:03:49,135 --> 00:03:50,102
Try walking.

89
00:03:50,102 --> 00:03:51,537
She's incredible.

90
00:03:53,506 --> 00:03:55,875
I told you there are masters.

91
00:03:56,209 --> 00:03:57,443
How can anyone not walk while doing this?

92
00:03:58,311 --> 00:04:01,914
(A belly dancer moves
with effortless ease.)

93
00:04:01,914 --> 00:04:05,151
Amazing.

94
00:04:05,384 --> 00:04:07,887
I thought, "I could win this."

95
00:04:08,254 --> 00:04:10,056
When it comes to hula hooping,

96
00:04:10,056 --> 00:04:12,325
I usually do it
for one or two hours at home.

97
00:04:12,325 --> 00:04:13,559
It's basically my specialty.

98
00:04:13,559 --> 00:04:14,827
She's so good.

99
00:04:15,194 --> 00:04:17,163
We should make her walk backward.

100
00:04:18,164 --> 00:04:20,499
We'll now begin the men's mothers' race.

101
00:04:21,267 --> 00:04:22,435
Ready.

102
00:04:22,969 --> 00:04:25,972
(Go)

103
00:04:28,708 --> 00:04:29,976
Look.

104
00:04:29,976 --> 00:04:31,611
That's it. Take it easy.

105
00:04:32,378 --> 00:04:33,579
You got this.

106
00:04:33,579 --> 00:04:34,547
You got this.

107
00:04:35,715 --> 00:04:36,983
She's amazing.

108
00:04:36,983 --> 00:04:38,584
My goodness. Look at that.

109
00:04:38,584 --> 00:04:40,186
She's incredible.

110
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,488
Amazing.

111
00:04:44,156 --> 00:04:45,124
Unbelievable.

112
00:04:45,124 --> 00:04:46,959
But that's so hard.

113
00:04:49,395 --> 00:04:50,963
(In Kwon's mother drops her hoop.)

114
00:04:50,963 --> 00:04:51,998
No.

115
00:04:53,332 --> 00:04:57,570
(Who will win?)

116
00:04:59,906 --> 00:05:01,374
(First place is Kwon Ye Chan's mother.)

117
00:05:01,374 --> 00:05:02,508
Of course.

118
00:05:02,508 --> 00:05:04,610
- I knew it.
- She didn't drop it once.

119
00:05:06,078 --> 00:05:09,682
(Second place is Kim Dong Young's mother.)

120
00:05:10,416 --> 00:05:12,485
Ye Chan's mother came in first.

121
00:05:12,485 --> 00:05:14,587
No one can beat belly dancing.

122
00:05:14,954 --> 00:05:16,722
I'll announce the results
of the men's mothers' race.

123
00:05:16,722 --> 00:05:19,192
First place goes to Kwon Ye Chan's mother.

124
00:05:22,895 --> 00:05:25,431
Second place goes to
Kim Dong Young's mother.

125
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:31,871
The mothers who earned
a private conversation are...

126
00:05:31,871 --> 00:05:33,406
Choi Jeong Yoon's mother,

127
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:35,608
Ahn Do Yoon's mother,

128
00:05:36,309 --> 00:05:39,545
Kwon Ye Chan's mother,
and Kim Dong Young's mother.

129
00:05:41,113 --> 00:05:42,281
Thank you.

130
00:05:42,281 --> 00:05:44,417
I wasn't much help, In Kwon.

131
00:05:44,417 --> 00:05:46,152
Well done.

132
00:05:46,152 --> 00:05:48,721
You're on your own now, just like before.

133
00:05:48,721 --> 00:05:49,822
She was in a league of her own.

134
00:05:51,123 --> 00:05:54,260
(The mothers' fiery competition ends.)

135
00:05:55,161 --> 00:05:56,929
- Mother.
- Yes?

136
00:05:56,929 --> 00:05:58,497
- I'm back.
- Okay.

137
00:05:59,665 --> 00:06:00,967
How was it?

138
00:06:00,967 --> 00:06:03,970
I'm exhausted. I could sleep right now.

139
00:06:03,970 --> 00:06:04,770
Was it fun?

140
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:07,073
You are now known
as the man who goes all in.

141
00:06:07,974 --> 00:06:10,042
But I haven't even talked
to the others yet.

142
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:12,345
You said you were interested
in only one woman earlier.

143
00:06:12,345 --> 00:06:15,381
That's better than saying two
and leaving things ambiguous.

144
00:06:15,815 --> 00:06:16,983
Goodness.

145
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:20,987
Maybe that two-on-one date...

146
00:06:20,987 --> 00:06:23,022
gave me a terrible headache.

147
00:06:23,022 --> 00:06:24,390
Because it was two-on-one?

148
00:06:24,390 --> 00:06:26,125
Because you talked so much?

149
00:06:26,125 --> 00:06:27,827
It wasn't so much the talking.

150
00:06:27,827 --> 00:06:30,530
I think it was the stress.
The mental strain.

151
00:06:30,530 --> 00:06:31,964
The pressure and all that.

152
00:06:31,964 --> 00:06:34,200
- Yesterday was the opposite.
- Don't overthink it.

153
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:35,902
Yesterday was really fun, though.

154
00:06:35,902 --> 00:06:39,238
It's not about taking it
lightly or seriously.

155
00:06:39,238 --> 00:06:40,573
It wasn't exactly pressure,

156
00:06:40,573 --> 00:06:41,641
but I felt pressured.

157
00:06:42,341 --> 00:06:45,044
It wasn't a high-pressure situation,
but I still felt it.

158
00:06:45,044 --> 00:06:46,045
I get what he means.

159
00:06:46,779 --> 00:06:49,015
Dating several people at once...

160
00:06:49,015 --> 00:06:50,283
is scary and hard.

161
00:06:51,617 --> 00:06:54,787
Jeong Yoon and I talked a lot.

162
00:06:54,787 --> 00:06:56,122
(Ha Yoon returns from the 3-on-1 date.)

163
00:06:56,122 --> 00:06:57,423
It wasn't uncomfortable at all.

164
00:06:57,423 --> 00:06:59,592
And we shared...

165
00:07:00,593 --> 00:07:02,728
more about ourselves than I expected.

166
00:07:02,728 --> 00:07:04,931
- Really?
- We shared a lot of thoughts too.

167
00:07:05,198 --> 00:07:08,434
But I still have no idea who Ye Chan...

168
00:07:09,135 --> 00:07:12,405
likes the most.

169
00:07:12,405 --> 00:07:13,673
But I don't think it's me.

170
00:07:15,341 --> 00:07:17,310
- Really?
- Yes.

171
00:07:18,544 --> 00:07:20,680
As we were coming back,

172
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,982
after we parked and started walking in,

173
00:07:22,982 --> 00:07:25,184
we ran into Dong Young and In Kwon.

174
00:07:26,619 --> 00:07:28,254
(Ye Chan's group returns from their date.)

175
00:07:28,254 --> 00:07:29,822
If we keep crossing paths like this...

176
00:07:29,822 --> 00:07:30,890
- What's this?
- What?

177
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:31,924
What's going on?

178
00:07:31,924 --> 00:07:33,025
Where are they going?

179
00:07:33,025 --> 00:07:34,861
(Everyone is flustered.)

180
00:07:34,861 --> 00:07:36,195
There goes the king of the ladies.

181
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:38,998
Shouldn't we avoid
running into each other?

182
00:07:39,866 --> 00:07:41,000
Maybe...

183
00:07:42,869 --> 00:07:45,504
What if they think we came to greet them?

184
00:07:45,504 --> 00:07:46,606
But that's not it.

185
00:07:47,206 --> 00:07:48,774
You look far too pleased with yourself.

186
00:07:49,008 --> 00:07:51,811
- Hello.
- Where are you going?

187
00:07:51,811 --> 00:07:54,280
We're going to get the bags from the car.

188
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:55,348
We're just carrying the bags.

189
00:07:55,348 --> 00:07:57,650
(Awkward laugh)

190
00:07:57,650 --> 00:07:58,851
That's awkward.

191
00:07:58,851 --> 00:08:00,353
That must be incredibly awkward.

192
00:08:01,821 --> 00:08:03,956
I just couldn't keep a straight face.

193
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,395
I should go talk to him.

194
00:08:11,097 --> 00:08:14,200
(Meanwhile,)

195
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:17,770
(the mothers secretly arrive
for their private conversations.)

196
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:21,107
I'm dying to know who they chose.

197
00:08:24,076 --> 00:08:30,583
(A chance to ask everything
they've wanted to know)

198
00:08:31,784 --> 00:08:35,588
(Do Yoon's mother
diligently checks her questions.)

199
00:08:36,489 --> 00:08:40,059
(Which man did Do Yoon's mother call?)

200
00:08:40,693 --> 00:08:42,094
(Private conversation request,
Ahn Do Yoon's mother chooses Ye Chan.)

201
00:08:42,094 --> 00:08:44,897
- Ye Chan.
- Ye Chan.

202
00:08:45,264 --> 00:08:46,532
His popularity...

203
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:50,102
- never lets up.
- The mothers love him.

204
00:08:51,204 --> 00:08:52,905
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

205
00:08:53,206 --> 00:08:55,408
- I won the game.
- Congratulations.

206
00:08:55,408 --> 00:08:56,842
So I earned this special privilege.

207
00:08:56,842 --> 00:08:58,744
Congratulations.

208
00:08:58,744 --> 00:08:59,812
How did the date go?

209
00:09:00,813 --> 00:09:02,582
We talked much more naturally
than I expected.

210
00:09:02,582 --> 00:09:03,482
Thank you.

211
00:09:04,650 --> 00:09:05,885
With three women?

212
00:09:06,485 --> 00:09:07,653
Yes, all three of them.

213
00:09:07,653 --> 00:09:08,554
It's okay.

214
00:09:09,655 --> 00:09:10,723
What did you eat?

215
00:09:10,723 --> 00:09:13,092
We had something like brunch.

216
00:09:13,092 --> 00:09:15,995
We had pasta, salad, and pizza.

217
00:09:15,995 --> 00:09:17,063
I see.

218
00:09:19,398 --> 00:09:20,333
Did you have fun?

219
00:09:21,234 --> 00:09:23,302
Yes, well, there were several of us...

220
00:09:23,302 --> 00:09:26,439
(Gulp)

221
00:09:26,439 --> 00:09:28,107
Even a lawyer gets nervous.

222
00:09:28,107 --> 00:09:29,175
Right.

223
00:09:29,775 --> 00:09:35,414
I'd like to know
what you think of Do Yoon.

224
00:09:35,414 --> 00:09:37,884
Do Yoon is...

225
00:09:37,884 --> 00:09:39,418
one of the three women...

226
00:09:39,418 --> 00:09:43,222
I'm interested in out of the five,

227
00:09:43,222 --> 00:09:45,825
and I'd like to talk more
and get to know her better.

228
00:09:45,825 --> 00:09:47,593
- Really?
- Yes.

229
00:09:47,593 --> 00:09:48,661
That's a relief.

230
00:09:49,495 --> 00:09:54,467
She's my daughter,
but even I can only guess.

231
00:09:54,467 --> 00:09:56,802
She seems quite interested in you.

232
00:09:56,802 --> 00:09:57,603
Do Yoon is interested in me?

233
00:09:57,603 --> 00:10:00,172
- Do Yoon likes you.
- I see.

234
00:10:00,172 --> 00:10:01,741
So,

235
00:10:01,741 --> 00:10:05,077
first, about Do Yoon...

236
00:10:05,077 --> 00:10:06,979
Her fa... Did she mention her family?

237
00:10:06,979 --> 00:10:08,281
- No.
- About her family.

238
00:10:08,281 --> 00:10:10,216
- No, not in detail.
- You didn't, right?

239
00:10:10,216 --> 00:10:14,186
Do Yoon's father has been a dentist
for many years,

240
00:10:14,186 --> 00:10:17,523
and he's still practicing.

241
00:10:17,523 --> 00:10:19,125
That's a strong selling point.

242
00:10:19,125 --> 00:10:22,228
Do you know why that's important?

243
00:10:22,228 --> 00:10:26,232
Suppose you marry someone whose family...

244
00:10:26,232 --> 00:10:29,001
- is struggling financially.
- Right.

245
00:10:29,001 --> 00:10:32,772
You might start worrying,

246
00:10:32,772 --> 00:10:34,273
"Will I need to keep supporting them?"

247
00:10:34,273 --> 00:10:38,544
She's making it clear...

248
00:10:38,544 --> 00:10:40,680
- that he needn't worry about her family.
- Exactly.

249
00:10:41,314 --> 00:10:44,350
Her father has been a dentist
for many years,

250
00:10:44,350 --> 00:10:47,687
and he's still practicing.

251
00:10:47,687 --> 00:10:50,923
Do Yoon's younger sibling...

252
00:10:50,923 --> 00:10:55,194
graduated from a teachers college
and now teaches elementary school.

253
00:10:55,194 --> 00:10:57,263
Family background is very important.

254
00:10:57,263 --> 00:10:58,931
Yes, absolutely.

255
00:10:59,165 --> 00:11:02,768
What about your family
and your father's work?

256
00:11:02,768 --> 00:11:06,973
I have a younger brother
who's four years younger.

257
00:11:06,973 --> 00:11:09,208
My parents are both alive and well,

258
00:11:09,208 --> 00:11:09,942
(She begins taking notes.)

259
00:11:09,942 --> 00:11:12,678
and they've run businesses for many years.

260
00:11:12,678 --> 00:11:18,084
They've been operating
postpartum care centers...

261
00:11:18,084 --> 00:11:21,220
since they first began
appearing in Korea...

262
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:22,355
Postpartum care centers.

263
00:11:22,355 --> 00:11:23,623
in the early 2000s,

264
00:11:23,623 --> 00:11:26,459
so for nearly 30 years now.

265
00:11:26,459 --> 00:11:29,061
Then you won't need to go
anywhere else later.

266
00:11:29,061 --> 00:11:30,329
They can go straight there.

267
00:11:30,329 --> 00:11:32,198
- Nice.
- And it'll be free too.

268
00:11:32,932 --> 00:11:37,303
They recently took something
like a sabbatical,

269
00:11:37,303 --> 00:11:40,673
and now they're preparing to reopen.

270
00:11:40,673 --> 00:11:41,874
Do they have their own brand?

271
00:11:42,775 --> 00:11:45,912
They didn't buy
into an existing franchise.

272
00:11:45,912 --> 00:11:46,779
They built their own brand.

273
00:11:46,779 --> 00:11:48,714
Their own brand, I see.

274
00:11:48,714 --> 00:11:52,919
At one point,
they ran about three locations at once.

275
00:11:52,919 --> 00:11:54,887
Did your mother run them with her husband?

276
00:11:54,887 --> 00:11:55,988
Yes, they ran them together.

277
00:11:57,356 --> 00:11:58,925
Then,

278
00:11:58,925 --> 00:12:01,527
once you complete your military service,

279
00:12:01,527 --> 00:12:05,198
where did you say you planned to go?

280
00:12:05,198 --> 00:12:09,202
I plan to join a law firm in Gangnam...

281
00:12:09,202 --> 00:12:10,269
or near the Seoul Central District Court.

282
00:12:10,269 --> 00:12:12,905
So you're going to work at a law firm,

283
00:12:12,905 --> 00:12:14,240
and learn the ropes there?

284
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:15,141
Yes.

285
00:12:16,175 --> 00:12:16,943
(The next question)

286
00:12:16,943 --> 00:12:20,213
Here's something else.

287
00:12:20,213 --> 00:12:25,885
If things worked out with Do Yoon,
how would you go...

288
00:12:25,885 --> 00:12:29,789
about deciding...

289
00:12:29,789 --> 00:12:32,124
where to live?

290
00:12:32,124 --> 00:12:34,260
But he said he already owns
a home in Yongsan.

291
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:36,395
He already owns a home.

292
00:12:36,395 --> 00:12:39,999
If you got a place in Dongtan...

293
00:12:39,999 --> 00:12:42,802
and the commute was manageable,

294
00:12:42,802 --> 00:12:46,639
you could later move to Seocho
or do it the other way around.

295
00:12:46,639 --> 00:12:50,776
Since Do Yoon is currently in Dongtan,

296
00:12:50,776 --> 00:12:52,378
that's what she's asking about.

297
00:12:52,378 --> 00:12:53,880
So, somewhere around there.

298
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,848
It would be a shame
for Do Yoon to give up her job.

299
00:12:56,949 --> 00:13:00,286
It's stable, she likes it,
and it suits her.

300
00:13:00,286 --> 00:13:03,322
The semiconductor processing work.

301
00:13:03,322 --> 00:13:06,526
What do you think about that?

302
00:13:06,526 --> 00:13:07,493
(Well...)

303
00:13:07,493 --> 00:13:09,061
That was something I started considering.

304
00:13:09,061 --> 00:13:11,898
I wanted to ask these questions,

305
00:13:11,898 --> 00:13:13,499
wondering whether you could do it.

306
00:13:14,934 --> 00:13:16,335
(Gulp)

307
00:13:16,335 --> 00:13:18,204
I've honestly never
considered this before in my life,

308
00:13:18,204 --> 00:13:20,907
so give me a moment to process it.

309
00:13:22,608 --> 00:13:25,811
Ultimately,

310
00:13:25,811 --> 00:13:30,550
one of my long-term goals...

311
00:13:30,550 --> 00:13:32,552
has been to settle in Yongsan or Gangnam.

312
00:13:32,552 --> 00:13:34,153
I believe that will happen.

313
00:13:34,787 --> 00:13:38,357
But on the way to that goal,

314
00:13:38,357 --> 00:13:40,026
living in Dongtan for a while...

315
00:13:40,026 --> 00:13:42,762
and commuting to Seocho...

316
00:13:42,762 --> 00:13:44,864
seems like something we could work out.

317
00:13:44,864 --> 00:13:47,133
It wouldn't have to be forever.

318
00:13:47,133 --> 00:13:49,168
You could always improve things...

319
00:13:49,168 --> 00:13:52,238
little by little.

320
00:13:52,238 --> 00:13:56,509
When I look at married couples around me,

321
00:13:56,509 --> 00:14:00,913
when one spouse has
a stable corporate job...

322
00:14:00,913 --> 00:14:03,216
and the other runs a business,

323
00:14:03,216 --> 00:14:06,786
they seem to build
a solid life together...

324
00:14:06,786 --> 00:14:09,355
well into their fifties and sixties.

325
00:14:09,355 --> 00:14:13,392
Since Do Yoon is very interested in you,

326
00:14:13,392 --> 00:14:16,629
please don't write her off
just because she's young.

327
00:14:17,730 --> 00:14:20,299
I'd never heard anything...

328
00:14:20,299 --> 00:14:22,301
even remotely like that in my life,

329
00:14:22,635 --> 00:14:24,270
so it caught me off guard.

330
00:14:25,605 --> 00:14:28,507
Still, Do Yoon's mother brought up...

331
00:14:28,507 --> 00:14:32,511
some very practical considerations.

332
00:14:32,511 --> 00:14:34,547
And some of her points made sense to me.

333
00:14:34,547 --> 00:14:35,882
It was a very rational perspective.

334
00:14:35,882 --> 00:14:36,782
So,

335
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:40,353
after hearing her out,

336
00:14:40,353 --> 00:14:43,456
I found my interest in Do Yoon growing.

337
00:14:44,357 --> 00:14:47,527
If you talk only about ideals,

338
00:14:47,527 --> 00:14:50,563
you may keep running into problems later.

339
00:14:50,563 --> 00:14:52,265
- Marriage is real life.
- Exactly.

340
00:14:54,066 --> 00:14:57,670
Jeong Yoon's mother chose Ye Chan earlier.

341
00:14:57,670 --> 00:15:00,573
Who did she choose this time?

342
00:15:00,573 --> 00:15:01,574
Ye Chan.

343
00:15:01,574 --> 00:15:04,510
Are we going to hear
Ye Chan's answers again?

344
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:05,778
Wait, different pants.

345
00:15:06,913 --> 00:15:10,416
(Who is the man in the unfamiliar pants
Jeong Yoon's mother called?)

346
00:15:10,416 --> 00:15:11,584
(It's Lee In Kwon.)

347
00:15:11,584 --> 00:15:13,252
- In Kwon.
- Ma'am.

348
00:15:13,252 --> 00:15:15,821
She must watch "Live Today" a lot.

349
00:15:15,821 --> 00:15:16,822
It's In Kwon.

350
00:15:16,822 --> 00:15:18,658
She really does watch "Live Today" often.

351
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:22,628
(Private conversation request,
Choi Jeong Yoon's mother chooses In Kwon.)

352
00:15:23,196 --> 00:15:26,065
I worked so hard earlier
just to talk to you.

353
00:15:26,065 --> 00:15:27,366
Thank you so much, ma'am.

354
00:15:30,069 --> 00:15:31,871
I never saw this coming.

355
00:15:31,871 --> 00:15:33,839
I really gave it my all.

356
00:15:33,839 --> 00:15:34,740
Thank you.

357
00:15:35,408 --> 00:15:38,010
I didn't see it coming at all,

358
00:15:38,010 --> 00:15:42,448
but Jeong Yoon's mother chose me
for her private conversation.

359
00:15:42,815 --> 00:15:45,084
It made me think,

360
00:15:45,084 --> 00:15:49,388
"So I'm her second choice."

361
00:15:50,356 --> 00:15:54,594
To be honest, when I chose earlier,

362
00:15:54,994 --> 00:15:57,630
I went back and forth for a long time.

363
00:15:58,297 --> 00:16:00,867
(Jeong Yoon's mother chose Ye Chan
after the men's introductions.)

364
00:16:00,867 --> 00:16:01,801
Thank you, ma'am.

365
00:16:02,568 --> 00:16:06,005
That's how torn I was,
so I really wanted to talk to you.

366
00:16:06,005 --> 00:16:07,907
- Thank you so much.
- Of course.

367
00:16:10,042 --> 00:16:12,411
Smile a little, will you?

368
00:16:12,411 --> 00:16:14,213
What's wrong with him?

369
00:16:14,213 --> 00:16:15,314
Why won't he smile?

370
00:16:16,115 --> 00:16:17,283
He's an announcer, for goodness' sake.

371
00:16:20,353 --> 00:16:22,855
I can ask you whatever I want, right?

372
00:16:22,855 --> 00:16:23,723
Yes.

373
00:16:24,857 --> 00:16:29,595
First, how do you feel about Jeong Yoon?

374
00:16:31,664 --> 00:16:34,300
Up until yesterday,

375
00:16:37,603 --> 00:16:39,038
I was very interested in her.

376
00:16:39,038 --> 00:16:39,972
Okay.

377
00:16:39,972 --> 00:16:43,943
Our lunch date was two-on-one,

378
00:16:43,943 --> 00:16:45,311
and so was dinner.

379
00:16:45,311 --> 00:16:47,179
That's just how things played out.

380
00:16:47,179 --> 00:16:48,848
He's talking nonsense again.

381
00:16:49,248 --> 00:16:50,316
(Holding back)

382
00:16:50,316 --> 00:16:52,518
This is driving me crazy.

383
00:16:53,486 --> 00:16:55,087
And as that kept happening,

384
00:16:56,188 --> 00:16:57,590
naturally,

385
00:16:58,558 --> 00:17:00,226
my interest in her...

386
00:17:00,226 --> 00:17:01,661
Really?

387
00:17:01,661 --> 00:17:04,197
I know it couldn't be helped,

388
00:17:04,197 --> 00:17:06,599
but honestly, my feelings cooled a little.

389
00:17:06,966 --> 00:17:09,869
He didn't have to be that honest.

390
00:17:09,869 --> 00:17:11,571
I mean, to her mother...

391
00:17:11,571 --> 00:17:14,207
He could've just said,
"I'm still interested."

392
00:17:14,207 --> 00:17:17,476
Doesn't he sound like he's sulking?
He sounds like that to me.

393
00:17:17,476 --> 00:17:18,844
Why would he be sulking?

394
00:17:18,844 --> 00:17:22,415
The way he's talking to her mother...

395
00:17:22,415 --> 00:17:24,116
makes it sound like a diplomatic summit.

396
00:17:24,116 --> 00:17:25,218
He's a little...

397
00:17:25,218 --> 00:17:26,552
What's wrong with him?

398
00:17:27,386 --> 00:17:29,355
Isn't he the oldest one here?

399
00:17:30,223 --> 00:17:31,624
What is he doing?

400
00:17:32,425 --> 00:17:35,962
If only he'd reversed the order.

401
00:17:35,962 --> 00:17:38,264
"I was disappointed
by how things unfolded,

402
00:17:38,264 --> 00:17:39,966
but I'm still interested in her."

403
00:17:39,966 --> 00:17:41,334
If only he'd said that.

404
00:17:41,334 --> 00:17:43,536
Even a 28-year-old knows better.

405
00:17:45,238 --> 00:17:47,373
Goodness.

406
00:17:47,773 --> 00:17:50,276
To be honest, my feelings cooled a little.

407
00:17:50,276 --> 00:17:52,144
I see.

408
00:17:52,144 --> 00:17:53,079
I understand.

409
00:17:56,582 --> 00:17:58,084
My goodness.

410
00:17:58,985 --> 00:18:00,086
Then,

411
00:18:01,187 --> 00:18:03,656
I feel like...

412
00:18:03,656 --> 00:18:05,758
I don't have much left to ask.

413
00:18:05,758 --> 00:18:07,493
See? Now she can't continue
the conversation.

414
00:18:07,493 --> 00:18:08,528
She has nothing else to say.

415
00:18:08,528 --> 00:18:11,497
The moment Jeong Yoon's mother heard that,
her interest in him...

416
00:18:11,497 --> 00:18:14,367
plummeted.

417
00:18:14,367 --> 00:18:16,068
- What a mess.
- What an idiot.

418
00:18:16,068 --> 00:18:18,638
Why would he be that honest there?

419
00:18:18,638 --> 00:18:21,274
But it's not like she dropped...

420
00:18:21,274 --> 00:18:24,410
from first to fifth place.

421
00:18:24,410 --> 00:18:25,678
She was first before, and...

422
00:18:25,678 --> 00:18:27,780
- And now she's second?
- Yes.

423
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:31,050
Why would he say that?

424
00:18:31,050 --> 00:18:33,452
Goodness.

425
00:18:33,452 --> 00:18:34,687
This is awful.

426
00:18:35,555 --> 00:18:37,523
Jeong Yoon actually...

427
00:18:37,523 --> 00:18:40,426
went by your room last night.

428
00:18:40,426 --> 00:18:41,961
You didn't know?

429
00:18:41,961 --> 00:18:45,064
She did go,

430
00:18:45,064 --> 00:18:46,132
but you weren't there.

431
00:18:47,099 --> 00:18:48,668
Is In Kwon there?

432
00:18:48,668 --> 00:18:49,669
He's out.

433
00:18:49,669 --> 00:18:51,404
- He went out?
- Yes.

434
00:18:52,371 --> 00:18:53,272
(Jeong Yoon and In Kwon
missed each other last night.)

435
00:18:53,272 --> 00:18:55,408
I guess his mother didn't tell him.

436
00:18:57,376 --> 00:18:58,444
I didn't...

437
00:18:58,444 --> 00:18:59,512
You didn't know?

438
00:18:59,512 --> 00:19:00,346
No.

439
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:05,351
Jeong Yoon was that interested in you,

440
00:19:05,351 --> 00:19:07,186
and I feel like I let her down.

441
00:19:07,186 --> 00:19:08,521
Why do you feel that way?

442
00:19:08,521 --> 00:19:10,756
I made the wrong call earlier.

443
00:19:10,756 --> 00:19:13,226
I thought it would be better...

444
00:19:13,226 --> 00:19:15,828
for Jeong Yoon to choose you
than for me to,

445
00:19:15,828 --> 00:19:17,363
so I held back.

446
00:19:17,797 --> 00:19:20,967
I worried there wouldn't be a chance
to undo that,

447
00:19:20,967 --> 00:19:22,201
so earlier,

448
00:19:22,201 --> 00:19:23,870
I hula-hooped
as if my life depended on it.

449
00:19:23,870 --> 00:19:24,904
She really did.

450
00:19:25,972 --> 00:19:27,406
I see.

451
00:19:27,406 --> 00:19:29,675
She felt so bad.

452
00:19:29,675 --> 00:19:31,210
That's why she did all that.

453
00:19:32,545 --> 00:19:33,546
Thank you so much.

454
00:19:33,546 --> 00:19:34,513
Not at all.

455
00:19:34,981 --> 00:19:36,382
We may have missed each other a lot,

456
00:19:37,149 --> 00:19:39,485
but we only need to
connect once in the end.

457
00:19:39,485 --> 00:19:40,653
Right.

458
00:19:42,421 --> 00:19:43,656
And I'll do my best to make that happen.

459
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:48,461
It's a shame
you don't quite fit that role,

460
00:19:48,461 --> 00:19:50,830
but I often say this to Jeong Yoon.

461
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:52,832
I ask her, "Are you Princess Pyeonggang?"

462
00:19:53,566 --> 00:19:59,005
She says she wants to meet
a foolish Ondal...

463
00:19:59,872 --> 00:20:02,542
and turn him into a great general.

464
00:20:02,542 --> 00:20:04,377
That makes my daughter
Princess Pyeonggang.

465
00:20:05,378 --> 00:20:07,513
My fortune says I'm destined to be Ondal,

466
00:20:07,513 --> 00:20:11,717
- that I'll thrive when I meet Pyeonggang.
- Really?

467
00:20:13,653 --> 00:20:15,087
Goodness.

468
00:20:15,087 --> 00:20:17,423
(Ondal In Kwon meets
Pyeonggang Jeong Yoon at the show.)

469
00:20:18,424 --> 00:20:20,159
After talking to her mother,

470
00:20:20,159 --> 00:20:21,994
my feelings for Jeong Yoon...

471
00:20:21,994 --> 00:20:23,696
changed dramatically...

472
00:20:23,696 --> 00:20:24,897
and grew much stronger.

473
00:20:25,865 --> 00:20:29,869
I thought I was the only one trying,

474
00:20:29,869 --> 00:20:31,204
so my feelings had cooled.

475
00:20:31,804 --> 00:20:34,540
But it turned out
to be a misunderstanding.

476
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:37,176
I found the energy...

477
00:20:37,176 --> 00:20:40,680
to give it another shot.

478
00:20:41,614 --> 00:20:44,283
I think this is exactly
when his feelings changed.

479
00:20:44,283 --> 00:20:46,686
When he learned
she'd gone looking for him.

480
00:20:46,686 --> 00:20:47,553
I see.

481
00:20:47,553 --> 00:20:49,488
That's probably when they shot up.

482
00:20:49,488 --> 00:20:51,958
- He looked genuinely surprised.
- Yes.

483
00:20:52,692 --> 00:20:55,228
(Who did Dong Young's mother choose?)

484
00:20:55,228 --> 00:20:57,063
Who do you think she'll choose?

485
00:20:57,063 --> 00:20:58,664
I think she'll choose that lady.

486
00:20:58,664 --> 00:21:00,233
- Ha Yoon?
- Ha Yoon.

487
00:21:00,766 --> 00:21:02,468
(Knock, knock)

488
00:21:02,468 --> 00:21:04,070
I'm coming in.

489
00:21:05,771 --> 00:21:07,006
Hello.

490
00:21:07,006 --> 00:21:07,974
Da Hye.

491
00:21:07,974 --> 00:21:09,308
(Kim Dong Young's mother chooses Da Hye.)

492
00:21:09,308 --> 00:21:10,276
How unexpected.

493
00:21:11,177 --> 00:21:14,981
Ha Yoon has talked
with Dong Young a lot already,

494
00:21:14,981 --> 00:21:20,586
so I thought it was a chance
to get to know someone else.

495
00:21:20,786 --> 00:21:23,089
Did you think I might call you?

496
00:21:23,089 --> 00:21:24,490
- No.
- You didn't, right?

497
00:21:24,490 --> 00:21:25,458
Not at all.

498
00:21:25,458 --> 00:21:29,462
Have you ever thought
about Dong Young that way?

499
00:21:29,462 --> 00:21:33,866
Our timing never worked out,
so we barely talked.

500
00:21:33,866 --> 00:21:37,003
I think I need to talk to him more first.

501
00:21:37,003 --> 00:21:37,904
Right?

502
00:21:38,371 --> 00:21:40,339
But I like you so much, ma'am.

503
00:21:40,339 --> 00:21:42,208
I really like your mother too.

504
00:21:42,208 --> 00:21:43,576
Exactly.

505
00:21:43,576 --> 00:21:46,646
It's fascinating.

506
00:21:46,646 --> 00:21:48,714
The mothers' chemistry matters too.

507
00:21:48,714 --> 00:21:51,384
And my mother got along so well with you.

508
00:21:51,384 --> 00:21:53,719
Knowing you were raised
by a woman like your mother,

509
00:21:53,719 --> 00:21:56,289
I thought, "I'd have nothing
to worry about with Da Hye."

510
00:21:56,289 --> 00:21:57,623
Thank you so much.

511
00:21:57,623 --> 00:22:00,960
My mother is helping me so much here.

512
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:02,795
You're beautiful too.

513
00:22:02,795 --> 00:22:03,763
Thank you so much.

514
00:22:03,763 --> 00:22:06,499
That may be the best compliment
I've ever received.

515
00:22:06,499 --> 00:22:09,235
And Dong Young...

516
00:22:09,235 --> 00:22:11,571
seems like a very thoughtful son.

517
00:22:11,571 --> 00:22:13,272
He loves making plans.

518
00:22:13,272 --> 00:22:16,075
If a new café opens
or he hears about a good bakery,

519
00:22:16,075 --> 00:22:18,811
- he always takes me there.
- He remembers it.

520
00:22:18,811 --> 00:22:20,846
He'll make time for it,

521
00:22:20,846 --> 00:22:23,316
and he comes home
the moment he gets off work.

522
00:22:23,316 --> 00:22:24,283
Surprisingly.

523
00:22:24,283 --> 00:22:28,287
People often misjudge him
because he works in sales.

524
00:22:28,287 --> 00:22:31,791
The job gives him
and a comfortable income.

525
00:22:31,791 --> 00:22:35,728
He may be an even better catch
than a doctor or lawyer.

526
00:22:35,728 --> 00:22:39,665
You should've included all that
in his introduction.

527
00:22:39,665 --> 00:22:42,935
I'm grateful you're sharing all this
with only me, but...

528
00:22:42,935 --> 00:22:45,338
She's so warm and friendly with her.

529
00:22:45,338 --> 00:22:46,339
She's very personable.

530
00:22:46,339 --> 00:22:48,875
I'm honestly so grateful.

531
00:22:48,875 --> 00:22:52,712
Would you be open
to a long-distance relationship?

532
00:22:52,712 --> 00:22:55,514
Actually, a long-distance relationship...

533
00:22:55,514 --> 00:22:58,684
might suit my lifestyle better.

534
00:22:58,684 --> 00:23:01,621
Even if we lived nearby,
I couldn't see him much on weekdays.

535
00:23:01,621 --> 00:23:04,223
What worries me is that...

536
00:23:04,223 --> 00:23:08,761
when I have some breathing room,
I can stay in touch often.

537
00:23:08,761 --> 00:23:12,899
But if we were long distance
during a busy period,

538
00:23:12,899 --> 00:23:17,570
we might both feel lonely.

539
00:23:17,570 --> 00:23:20,773
If he weren't nearby
and I wasn't staying in touch,

540
00:23:20,773 --> 00:23:23,876
that's what I'd worry about, honestly.

541
00:23:23,876 --> 00:23:25,311
That's manageable.

542
00:23:26,078 --> 00:23:28,381
Everything about you sounds wonderful.
You have so many good qualities.

543
00:23:28,381 --> 00:23:29,215
Not at all.

544
00:23:29,849 --> 00:23:33,219
I couldn't shake the feeling
that you'd be a great match.

545
00:23:33,219 --> 00:23:34,854
I couldn't say that to Dong Young, though.

546
00:23:34,854 --> 00:23:35,855
I see.

547
00:23:35,855 --> 00:23:39,692
But I thought
it might be nice if you two talked.

548
00:23:39,692 --> 00:23:42,428
Once you approach someone
and start talking,

549
00:23:42,428 --> 00:23:44,830
you start building rapport.

550
00:23:45,698 --> 00:23:46,999
She was very open to it.

551
00:23:46,999 --> 00:23:49,368
You can see
her mother's best qualities in her.

552
00:23:49,368 --> 00:23:52,471
She was clearly raised well.

553
00:23:52,772 --> 00:23:58,411
I'd love to see her and Dong Young
build something from here.

554
00:23:58,411 --> 00:24:00,046
I liked everything about her.

555
00:24:01,814 --> 00:24:05,351
The mothers are opening
new doors for their sons.

556
00:24:06,519 --> 00:24:08,154
Da Hye speaks so well too.

557
00:24:08,154 --> 00:24:09,789
She's so warm and friendly.

558
00:24:09,789 --> 00:24:11,257
From a mother's perspective,

559
00:24:11,257 --> 00:24:14,227
imagine your future daughter-in-law...

560
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:17,263
sitting there without saying a word,

561
00:24:17,263 --> 00:24:19,098
then quietly getting up and leaving.

562
00:24:19,098 --> 00:24:20,666
Honestly,

563
00:24:20,666 --> 00:24:23,636
you'd rather she felt at ease around you.

564
00:24:23,636 --> 00:24:27,406
I personally envy
that kind of personality.

565
00:24:27,406 --> 00:24:30,176
I'm not that kind of
daughter-in-law either.

566
00:24:30,176 --> 00:24:32,044
I also tend to sit quietly
and leave quietly.

567
00:24:32,044 --> 00:24:33,212
Just looking at you,

568
00:24:33,212 --> 00:24:36,115
I can easily imagine that.

569
00:24:36,115 --> 00:24:39,051
But if I ever have a daughter-in-law,

570
00:24:39,051 --> 00:24:41,587
I think I'd want someone like her.

571
00:24:41,587 --> 00:24:44,056
- Really?
- It's so strange, but yes.

572
00:24:44,056 --> 00:24:45,091
I should ask my mom too.

573
00:24:45,091 --> 00:24:47,026
Ask her. I'm serious.

574
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:51,097
(Which woman did Ye Chan's mother choose?)

575
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:52,298
I think Jeong Yoon.

576
00:24:52,298 --> 00:24:53,733
I was just thinking that too.

577
00:24:55,835 --> 00:24:59,472
(Whom did the mother
of the 3-vote man choose?)

578
00:24:59,472 --> 00:25:02,275
Hello, ma'am.

579
00:25:02,842 --> 00:25:05,444
(Private conversation request,
Kwon Ye Chan's mother chooses Da Hye.)

580
00:25:05,444 --> 00:25:06,212
How unexpected.

581
00:25:06,212 --> 00:25:07,780
She chose Da Hye.

582
00:25:08,581 --> 00:25:12,652
Da Hye shares our faith,

583
00:25:12,652 --> 00:25:16,889
and Ye Chan has shown
continued interest in her,

584
00:25:16,889 --> 00:25:20,026
so I wanted to talk with her more closely.

585
00:25:20,026 --> 00:25:22,528
There were things I wanted to ask.

586
00:25:22,528 --> 00:25:27,767
One-on-one, we could talk
without worrying about anyone else.

587
00:25:28,167 --> 00:25:30,570
She was an unexpected favorite.

588
00:25:30,570 --> 00:25:32,572
She really was.

589
00:25:32,572 --> 00:25:34,273
She's clearly the mothers' favorite.

590
00:25:34,273 --> 00:25:35,741
She definitely is.

591
00:25:35,741 --> 00:25:37,877
And Shin Woo made his feelings
too obvious.

592
00:25:37,877 --> 00:25:39,378
He came on so strong.

593
00:25:39,378 --> 00:25:43,482
He made it crystal clear
that Da Hye was the only one for him.

594
00:25:43,482 --> 00:25:47,220
Now that I have this chance,
I wanted to ask about it.

595
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:49,789
This is great. I love it.

596
00:25:49,789 --> 00:25:54,827
If you were to get married,

597
00:25:54,827 --> 00:25:55,795
are you ready?

598
00:25:55,795 --> 00:25:58,831
Emotionally, I mean.

599
00:25:58,831 --> 00:26:01,667
Honestly, if you connect with someone,

600
00:26:01,667 --> 00:26:05,705
relationships progress very quickly.
I've seen that many times.

601
00:26:05,705 --> 00:26:09,842
I've also seen many couples marry quickly
and live very happily,

602
00:26:09,842 --> 00:26:15,414
so ultimately, chemistry and marriage...

603
00:26:15,681 --> 00:26:18,551
seem to unfold naturally
when they're meant to.

604
00:26:18,551 --> 00:26:21,787
I don't think I could predict
how it would happen for me.

605
00:26:21,787 --> 00:26:22,555
Then,

606
00:26:23,256 --> 00:26:26,025
you knew Ye Chan...

607
00:26:26,025 --> 00:26:28,160
was interested in three women, right?

608
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:29,595
When he told us earlier...

609
00:26:29,595 --> 00:26:31,531
- Did you learn then?
- Yes.

610
00:26:31,531 --> 00:26:33,032
Well,

611
00:26:33,032 --> 00:26:35,067
the truth is,

612
00:26:35,067 --> 00:26:36,602
you are one of those three.

613
00:26:36,602 --> 00:26:37,737
Really?

614
00:26:37,737 --> 00:26:39,272
I genuinely had no idea.

615
00:26:39,272 --> 00:26:40,673
I never expected that.

616
00:26:40,673 --> 00:26:41,841
- Really?
- Not at all.

617
00:26:41,841 --> 00:26:47,747
So my thinking is actually
along the same lines.

618
00:26:48,114 --> 00:26:49,348
But...

619
00:26:49,715 --> 00:26:51,751
I heard something earlier today...

620
00:26:51,751 --> 00:26:54,353
when the mothers were talking.

621
00:26:54,353 --> 00:26:57,990
They said certain people
were basically set on each other.

622
00:26:57,990 --> 00:26:59,892
- That's what people say.
- Things like that.

623
00:27:00,593 --> 00:27:02,929
They said number three and number four
are already set.

624
00:27:02,929 --> 00:27:03,863
Really?

625
00:27:04,530 --> 00:27:06,699
Even the participants knew.

626
00:27:06,699 --> 00:27:07,733
Seriously?

627
00:27:08,801 --> 00:27:09,735
Wait.

628
00:27:10,203 --> 00:27:12,038
- The ladies know too?
- Yes.

629
00:27:12,038 --> 00:27:13,773
- They all know?
- Yes, all of them.

630
00:27:13,773 --> 00:27:15,374
I see.

631
00:27:16,375 --> 00:27:17,743
So...

632
00:27:17,743 --> 00:27:21,647
(Ye Chan's mother thought
Da Hye had made up her mind.)

633
00:27:21,647 --> 00:27:25,351
Now that I've heard that,
everything makes sense.

634
00:27:25,351 --> 00:27:28,854
I never refused
to talk to anyone who approached me.

635
00:27:28,854 --> 00:27:32,892
From the outside,
I talked easily to that man who came over,

636
00:27:32,892 --> 00:27:35,461
so I can see why it looked that way.

637
00:27:35,461 --> 00:27:36,629
That doesn't mean
I'm not interested in him.

638
00:27:36,629 --> 00:27:39,332
He is one of the men I'm interested in,

639
00:27:39,332 --> 00:27:42,301
but I'm not set on charging
straight ahead with him.

640
00:27:42,301 --> 00:27:44,937
Of the two men I'm interested in,

641
00:27:44,937 --> 00:27:46,672
one is Ye Chan.

642
00:27:46,672 --> 00:27:50,810
I'd actually been thinking...

643
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:54,447
that I wanted to talk
to Ye Chan again today.

644
00:27:54,447 --> 00:27:57,650
I didn't come here
only to spare other people's feelings.

645
00:27:57,650 --> 00:27:59,418
Consideration matters,

646
00:27:59,418 --> 00:28:02,488
but I'm also here
to meet someone for myself.

647
00:28:02,488 --> 00:28:05,825
So I'm trying to make
the most of every situation.

648
00:28:06,592 --> 00:28:10,329
I was so grateful...

649
00:28:10,329 --> 00:28:12,198
that both mothers chose me...

650
00:28:12,198 --> 00:28:13,566
and gave me a chance to talk.

651
00:28:13,566 --> 00:28:17,103
I thought my mother
probably had a lot to do with it.

652
00:28:17,670 --> 00:28:21,073
Could the talks with the mothers
change her feelings?

653
00:28:21,073 --> 00:28:23,242
I think they definitely will.

654
00:28:23,242 --> 00:28:24,644
Until now,

655
00:28:24,644 --> 00:28:27,213
Shin Woo was the only man
who'd picked her first.

656
00:28:27,213 --> 00:28:29,048
- Exactly.
- So she may have thought,

657
00:28:29,048 --> 00:28:32,785
"I guess no one else is interested in me."
But now,

658
00:28:32,785 --> 00:28:33,753
"Wait."

659
00:28:34,287 --> 00:28:36,756
"I never knew
I was an unexpected favorite."

660
00:28:36,756 --> 00:28:37,823
Exactly.

661
00:28:37,823 --> 00:28:41,093
"Why should I put all my eggs
in one basket?"

662
00:28:41,093 --> 00:28:44,664
"I could start looking around."

663
00:28:44,664 --> 00:28:46,132
This could get interesting.

664
00:28:46,132 --> 00:28:50,770
A love triangle between the lawyer
and the doctor of Korean medicine.

665
00:28:51,804 --> 00:28:54,273
Shin Woo stopped by earlier.

666
00:28:55,474 --> 00:28:57,777
Your neck kept bothering you,

667
00:28:58,644 --> 00:29:00,179
so he left you a pain relief patch.

668
00:29:00,179 --> 00:29:01,581
He did?

669
00:29:01,581 --> 00:29:02,582
Yes.

670
00:29:03,316 --> 00:29:04,483
Is Da Hye there?

671
00:29:04,483 --> 00:29:05,451
Da Hye?

672
00:29:05,451 --> 00:29:06,619
Yes, is she here?

673
00:29:06,619 --> 00:29:08,287
Da Hye said she'd hurt her neck.

674
00:29:08,287 --> 00:29:09,589
Right.

675
00:29:09,589 --> 00:29:10,756
I was worried.

676
00:29:10,756 --> 00:29:12,825
A pain relief patch. Will this help?

677
00:29:12,825 --> 00:29:14,227
That's the doctor of Korean medicine.

678
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:17,196
Shin Woo left this for me?
That's so thoughtful.

679
00:29:17,196 --> 00:29:18,564
It really does feel cool.

680
00:29:21,234 --> 00:29:22,335
Are you worn out? Lie down.

681
00:29:23,736 --> 00:29:25,838
I don't know why I keep tearing up,

682
00:29:25,838 --> 00:29:28,407
but I can't stop.
Could you bring me some tissues?

683
00:29:28,741 --> 00:29:30,009
What's wrong all of a sudden?

684
00:29:31,177 --> 00:29:32,612
- What brought this on?
- Why are you crying?

685
00:29:33,145 --> 00:29:34,280
But this...

686
00:29:34,280 --> 00:29:36,249
Isn't that
the happiest situation possible?

687
00:29:36,249 --> 00:29:37,884
- She must be so happy.
- She's crying because she's so happy.

688
00:29:37,884 --> 00:29:39,685
- Are those tears of joy?
- Yes, probably.

689
00:29:39,685 --> 00:29:41,687
Maybe being showered with affection
so suddenly...

690
00:29:41,687 --> 00:29:43,723
- has left her overwhelmed.
- Really?

691
00:29:43,723 --> 00:29:45,791
"Do I deserve to be loved this much?"

692
00:29:47,493 --> 00:29:48,361
Why?

693
00:29:49,629 --> 00:29:53,232
I don't know why I'm crying either.

694
00:29:56,636 --> 00:29:57,737
The tears just keep coming.

695
00:30:04,877 --> 00:30:06,979
I guess all these thoughts hit me at once.

696
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:08,948
That can happen.

697
00:30:11,117 --> 00:30:14,153
The men's mothers had a first
and second place too, right?

698
00:30:14,654 --> 00:30:16,122
Ye Chan's mother came in first.

699
00:30:17,023 --> 00:30:18,558
Dong Young's mother came in second.

700
00:30:18,558 --> 00:30:20,426
I met both of them.

701
00:30:21,861 --> 00:30:23,629
- They both chose you?
- Yes.

702
00:30:24,430 --> 00:30:26,933
My goodness. I'm grateful.

703
00:30:26,933 --> 00:30:28,267
I was so grateful.

704
00:30:28,267 --> 00:30:29,702
They even asked...

705
00:30:29,702 --> 00:30:33,139
if their questions sounded rude,
but I was genuinely fine.

706
00:30:33,139 --> 00:30:34,040
I see.

707
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:39,011
Maybe I was so drained
that it came out as tears.

708
00:30:39,011 --> 00:30:40,479
- Right.
- She was drained,

709
00:30:40,479 --> 00:30:42,648
and she cried because of that?

710
00:30:42,648 --> 00:30:45,751
Dealing with the mothers
must have been hard.

711
00:30:45,751 --> 00:30:47,920
But she was grateful too.

712
00:30:49,622 --> 00:30:52,658
I keep thinking about Ye Chan.

713
00:30:52,658 --> 00:30:55,461
I also...

714
00:30:55,461 --> 00:30:58,698
wanted to talk to Ye Chan...

715
00:30:59,432 --> 00:31:00,833
one more time.

716
00:31:00,833 --> 00:31:03,269
I've felt that way since this morning.

717
00:31:03,269 --> 00:31:07,573
At the same time, when I talk to Shin Woo,

718
00:31:07,573 --> 00:31:12,378
I can see how sincere and kind he is.

719
00:31:12,378 --> 00:31:13,279
But...

720
00:31:14,614 --> 00:31:18,217
there are still a few things
giving me pause.

721
00:31:18,217 --> 00:31:20,519
I can't explain all of them,

722
00:31:20,519 --> 00:31:22,221
because they're about how I feel...

723
00:31:22,221 --> 00:31:25,591
when I imagine
a romantic relationship with him.

724
00:31:25,591 --> 00:31:29,061
There are several things like that.

725
00:31:30,296 --> 00:31:34,600
I've been thinking about them a lot.

726
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:35,835
(She has more and more doubts
about her relationship with Shin Woo.)

727
00:31:35,835 --> 00:31:39,171
Maybe it was because Shin Woo said
I was his only choice.

728
00:31:39,171 --> 00:31:40,873
I don't know,

729
00:31:41,173 --> 00:31:45,711
but I spent a lot of time
thinking about...

730
00:31:45,711 --> 00:31:47,613
how I should act around him.

731
00:31:48,347 --> 00:31:49,649
At the moment, there's one person.

732
00:31:54,954 --> 00:31:57,523
They said you and him...

733
00:31:57,523 --> 00:32:00,560
only had eyes for each other.

734
00:32:02,528 --> 00:32:05,231
Now all the pieces fit,

735
00:32:05,231 --> 00:32:08,834
and I realized how oblivious I was.

736
00:32:09,468 --> 00:32:11,571
"I can't stay stuck here."

737
00:32:11,571 --> 00:32:14,607
"I need to explore a bigger world."

738
00:32:14,607 --> 00:32:15,975
"But before I leave..."

739
00:32:15,975 --> 00:32:18,678
You know how you get a little teary...

740
00:32:18,678 --> 00:32:23,282
saying goodbye to a friend
you've been through things with?

741
00:32:23,282 --> 00:32:24,383
It's gratitude.

742
00:32:24,383 --> 00:32:26,252
That's exactly it.

743
00:32:27,086 --> 00:32:28,120
Goodness.

744
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:29,589
Good job, son.

745
00:32:30,656 --> 00:32:31,791
Goodness.

746
00:32:33,526 --> 00:32:35,094
How did it go?

747
00:32:35,094 --> 00:32:36,696
I went on a group date.

748
00:32:36,696 --> 00:32:38,865
A group date is draining, isn't it?

749
00:32:38,865 --> 00:32:40,867
It was, but then...

750
00:32:41,100 --> 00:32:43,336
they said I had something else to do.

751
00:32:43,336 --> 00:32:44,537
What?

752
00:32:44,537 --> 00:32:46,239
A secret date?

753
00:32:46,239 --> 00:32:47,506
A private interview?

754
00:32:47,506 --> 00:32:49,242
Do Yoon's mother was waiting for me.

755
00:32:49,242 --> 00:32:50,676
- Do Yoon's mother?
- Yes.

756
00:32:50,676 --> 00:32:51,444
And?

757
00:32:51,444 --> 00:32:55,948
Her father is still practicing
as a dentist,

758
00:32:55,948 --> 00:32:57,984
and she asked
some very practical questions.

759
00:32:59,118 --> 00:33:02,588
Do Yoon works in Pyeongtaek
and lives in Dongtan.

760
00:33:02,588 --> 00:33:06,859
She asked
where we'd live if we got married.

761
00:33:06,859 --> 00:33:10,630
For instance,
I could get a place in Dongtan,

762
00:33:10,630 --> 00:33:12,198
Do Yoon could commute to Pyeongtaek,

763
00:33:12,198 --> 00:33:14,634
and I could commute
from Dongtan to Gangnam in Seoul.

764
00:33:15,401 --> 00:33:17,236
That would be rough.

765
00:33:17,236 --> 00:33:18,804
You hate long drives.

766
00:33:18,804 --> 00:33:22,408
I really thought about it as she spoke.

767
00:33:22,408 --> 00:33:24,644
And I came in first.

768
00:33:26,279 --> 00:33:27,313
Guess who I chose to talk with.

769
00:33:28,514 --> 00:33:29,582
Where's that notebook?

770
00:33:30,516 --> 00:33:33,686
The notebook again?
He must be taking more notes.

771
00:33:34,287 --> 00:33:36,022
(Here you go.)

772
00:33:36,222 --> 00:33:37,957
I talked with Da Hye.

773
00:33:38,457 --> 00:33:40,960
She said she was interested in two men.

774
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:44,697
They were you and Shin Woo.

775
00:33:45,765 --> 00:33:48,201
Da Hye really does seem great.

776
00:33:49,101 --> 00:33:52,505
So, how do you rank them now?

777
00:33:53,139 --> 00:33:55,708
Do Yoon, Da Hye, and Jeong Yoon.

778
00:33:56,409 --> 00:33:57,677
Right now, all three are...

779
00:33:59,345 --> 00:34:00,680
- tied for third.
- What?

780
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,181
- Really?
- Yes.

781
00:34:02,181 --> 00:34:05,585
At this rate,
he's going to go home in tears.

782
00:34:06,719 --> 00:34:09,288
What does tied for third even mean?

783
00:34:10,056 --> 00:34:12,158
Tied for third? Then who's first?

784
00:34:12,959 --> 00:34:13,926
There is no first or second.

785
00:34:13,926 --> 00:34:15,761
Tied for first or third, same difference.

786
00:34:16,562 --> 00:34:17,396
Really?

787
00:34:17,396 --> 00:34:20,199
Who do you think
Jeong Yoon's mother chose?

788
00:34:22,068 --> 00:34:23,035
I'm not sure.

789
00:34:24,503 --> 00:34:25,905
- You talked to him?
- Yes.

790
00:34:25,905 --> 00:34:27,406
Who did you talk to?

791
00:34:27,406 --> 00:34:28,274
In Kwon.

792
00:34:28,274 --> 00:34:29,375
I knew it.

793
00:34:30,443 --> 00:34:31,811
What did you talk about?

794
00:34:31,811 --> 00:34:34,313
I asked how he felt about you.

795
00:34:34,313 --> 00:34:36,649
- How he felt about me?
- Yes.

796
00:34:36,649 --> 00:34:39,418
Didn't he say he wasn't sure
because we barely talked?

797
00:34:39,418 --> 00:34:41,754
Right. You'd barely talked
and kept missing each other.

798
00:34:41,754 --> 00:34:43,923
He had no idea
you went looking for him last night.

799
00:34:43,923 --> 00:34:47,159
So he assumed you weren't interested.

800
00:34:47,159 --> 00:34:50,830
I think talking to him
and clearing it up was the right call.

801
00:34:50,830 --> 00:34:52,698
He seemed like a much better guy
than I expected.

802
00:34:53,766 --> 00:34:55,334
Here's what I'm thinking.

803
00:34:55,334 --> 00:34:57,970
It's not that I don't like Ye Chan.

804
00:34:57,970 --> 00:34:59,805
He seems like a good person.

805
00:34:59,805 --> 00:35:01,641
But if all of them are good people,

806
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:06,479
why should I have to overcome
a religious difference to date him?

807
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:08,748
Why go through that?
That's what I'm wondering.

808
00:35:08,748 --> 00:35:10,783
I could make the effort,

809
00:35:10,783 --> 00:35:12,885
but I don't have to.

810
00:35:12,885 --> 00:35:15,955
Exactly.
It's better to put that effort elsewhere.

811
00:35:16,756 --> 00:35:18,124
So...

812
00:35:18,124 --> 00:35:23,029
I think I should get to know
the other two first.

813
00:35:23,029 --> 00:35:24,597
- The other two men?
- Yes.

814
00:35:25,598 --> 00:35:26,999
Is anyone in there?

815
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:27,833
Yes.

816
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:30,203
Are you alone, ma'am?

817
00:35:31,404 --> 00:35:32,905
I came because my mom disappeared.

818
00:35:32,905 --> 00:35:34,840
Really? Your mother isn't here.

819
00:35:35,341 --> 00:35:38,044
Was it fun? How did it go?

820
00:35:38,311 --> 00:35:39,679
How was it?

821
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:40,713
Well...

822
00:35:40,713 --> 00:35:42,048
- My head hurt.
- Goodness.

823
00:35:42,048 --> 00:35:43,082
He's lying down too.

824
00:35:43,082 --> 00:35:45,184
Same, right?
I was completely drained earlier.

825
00:35:45,184 --> 00:35:45,918
He's...

826
00:35:45,918 --> 00:35:46,852
Come in.

827
00:35:47,420 --> 00:35:48,487
Come in.

828
00:35:49,722 --> 00:35:50,723
How did it go?

829
00:35:50,723 --> 00:35:51,958
(The men with 3 and 2 votes
from the mothers meet.)

830
00:35:51,958 --> 00:35:54,493
- The professionals.
- The two popular men are together.

831
00:35:54,493 --> 00:35:55,795
The professional alliance.

832
00:35:57,063 --> 00:36:00,066
How was it, Ye Chan? Give us the recap.

833
00:36:00,066 --> 00:36:01,868
The atmosphere was
much better than yesterday.

834
00:36:01,868 --> 00:36:03,636
- Better than yesterday?
- Yes.

835
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,505
So after seeing the three of them,

836
00:36:06,505 --> 00:36:11,110
did you like anyone
even just a little more?

837
00:36:11,110 --> 00:36:13,179
Did your feelings shift at all?

838
00:36:13,746 --> 00:36:15,014
Yes, ultimately,

839
00:36:15,014 --> 00:36:18,050
I was more curious
about Do Yoon and Jeong Yoon.

840
00:36:18,050 --> 00:36:19,452
Do Yoon and Jeong Yoon?

841
00:36:19,986 --> 00:36:22,054
- How was Do Yoon?
- Do Yoon?

842
00:36:22,054 --> 00:36:23,122
What do you find appealing about her?

843
00:36:23,956 --> 00:36:25,458
You end up
taking her mother into account too.

844
00:36:26,592 --> 00:36:28,561
My impression of her mother,

845
00:36:28,861 --> 00:36:32,331
and what I learned about her family.

846
00:36:32,999 --> 00:36:34,100
I mean that in a positive way.

847
00:36:34,500 --> 00:36:38,070
I thought I'd never be swayed
by those things,

848
00:36:38,070 --> 00:36:40,006
but they did get my attention.

849
00:36:40,006 --> 00:36:41,674
She comes from a solid family.

850
00:36:41,674 --> 00:36:45,111
I wouldn't have to
worry about that, at least.

851
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:49,782
Then, if you got a chance
to have dinner one-on-one,

852
00:36:49,782 --> 00:36:52,218
who would you ask to join you?

853
00:36:52,885 --> 00:36:54,954
Who would you like to talk to over dinner?

854
00:36:56,923 --> 00:36:58,524
Jeong Yoon or Da Hye.

855
00:36:59,158 --> 00:37:00,726
Jeong Yoon or Da Hye.

856
00:37:00,726 --> 00:37:02,662
Da Hye was mentioned.

857
00:37:03,262 --> 00:37:04,463
Da Hye.

858
00:37:04,463 --> 00:37:05,565
A love triangle.

859
00:37:05,932 --> 00:37:06,999
(Da Hye is unexpectedly mentioned.)

860
00:37:06,999 --> 00:37:10,970
I haven't had a proper one-on-one
with Jeong Yoon,

861
00:37:10,970 --> 00:37:13,639
and I've barely talked to Da Hye at all.

862
00:37:13,639 --> 00:37:14,707
Was I keeping her all to myself?

863
00:37:14,707 --> 00:37:16,409
No, that's not what I meant.

864
00:37:16,409 --> 00:37:19,345
Our timing just didn't line up.

865
00:37:19,345 --> 00:37:21,280
(Suddenly silent)

866
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,748
Look at that.

867
00:37:22,982 --> 00:37:24,650
- All of a sudden...
- It's so obvious.

868
00:37:24,650 --> 00:37:26,652
He suddenly has a rival.

869
00:37:27,186 --> 00:37:29,555
But why do I want...

870
00:37:29,555 --> 00:37:31,457
to talk to Da Hye again?

871
00:37:31,457 --> 00:37:33,459
My goodness.

872
00:37:34,227 --> 00:37:35,561
You're completely smitten.

873
00:37:35,561 --> 00:37:37,129
Am I?

874
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:38,197
Yes.

875
00:37:38,197 --> 00:37:41,434
After the two-on-one date,

876
00:37:41,434 --> 00:37:46,239
I wonder how she felt
and whether anything changed.

877
00:37:47,206 --> 00:37:48,641
Did she have a change of heart?

878
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:51,377
And who else did she meet?

879
00:37:54,914 --> 00:37:56,282
Tonight is crucial.

880
00:37:58,017 --> 00:37:58,885
That's right.

881
00:37:58,885 --> 00:38:01,187
At this point,

882
00:38:01,187 --> 00:38:03,222
Shin Woo should probably
back off for a bit.

883
00:38:03,222 --> 00:38:04,490
Right. That would be better.

884
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:07,093
Da Hye has been emotionally shaken...

885
00:38:07,093 --> 00:38:09,128
after both private conversations.

886
00:38:09,128 --> 00:38:11,731
If he charges in again now,
it may push her away.

887
00:38:11,731 --> 00:38:12,532
Right.

888
00:38:13,099 --> 00:38:16,669
(Meanwhile,
Ha Yoon goes looking for someone.)

889
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:18,170
Dong Young, do you have a minute?

890
00:38:18,170 --> 00:38:19,105
Yes.

891
00:38:20,206 --> 00:38:22,909
I came because I think we need to talk.

892
00:38:22,909 --> 00:38:23,910
Thanks.

893
00:38:23,910 --> 00:38:25,511
She went to see Dong Young.

894
00:38:26,145 --> 00:38:28,247
We just talked over there earlier.

895
00:38:28,514 --> 00:38:30,249
I know. And here we are again.

896
00:38:30,249 --> 00:38:31,017
Exactly.

897
00:38:31,017 --> 00:38:32,485
I...

898
00:38:33,252 --> 00:38:34,554
have something to talk through.

899
00:38:35,922 --> 00:38:37,623
- We heard your introduction.
- Right.

900
00:38:37,623 --> 00:38:42,762
But you live much, much farther south...

901
00:38:42,762 --> 00:38:44,830
than I expected.

902
00:38:45,198 --> 00:38:49,035
Have you spent much time
traveling to Seoul?

903
00:38:49,035 --> 00:38:50,069
For dating?

904
00:38:50,069 --> 00:38:52,171
Not necessarily for dating.

905
00:38:52,605 --> 00:38:55,474
I've traveled quite a bit.

906
00:38:55,474 --> 00:38:59,378
Even outside of dating,
I visit Seoul from time to time.

907
00:38:59,378 --> 00:39:00,780
I see.

908
00:39:01,847 --> 00:39:03,783
From my house,

909
00:39:03,783 --> 00:39:06,619
the airport is about 20 minutes away.

910
00:39:06,953 --> 00:39:09,889
Even taking the SRT from Busan Station,

911
00:39:09,889 --> 00:39:12,091
I can get to Seoul in under three hours.

912
00:39:13,226 --> 00:39:14,293
Honestly,

913
00:39:14,293 --> 00:39:16,963
once I heard "Gimhae,"
I stopped processing everything else.

914
00:39:16,963 --> 00:39:17,897
Really?

915
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:20,766
Was Gimhae that much of a shock?

916
00:39:20,766 --> 00:39:22,802
I just wrote "Gimhae"
over and over in my notes.

917
00:39:23,669 --> 00:39:25,271
Gimhae.

918
00:39:27,206 --> 00:39:30,142
I did say I could go anywhere
south of the 38th parallel.

919
00:39:30,142 --> 00:39:35,548
Personally, I don't think...

920
00:39:35,548 --> 00:39:38,618
time, distance,
or physical constraints matter much.

921
00:39:39,986 --> 00:39:42,021
That's how I feel.

922
00:39:42,021 --> 00:39:44,423
When I'm dating someone,

923
00:39:44,824 --> 00:39:48,094
I don't want them
to make a huge sacrifice for me.

924
00:39:48,094 --> 00:39:49,262
Because...

925
00:39:49,262 --> 00:39:52,698
when one person gives up too much,

926
00:39:52,698 --> 00:39:55,334
it can create...

927
00:39:55,334 --> 00:39:57,336
a difference in perspective.

928
00:39:57,770 --> 00:40:03,976
A relationship without that sacrifice
seems healthier.

929
00:40:07,813 --> 00:40:09,815
Before I opened my clinic,

930
00:40:09,815 --> 00:40:12,118
my job gave me
a great deal of freedom to relocate.

931
00:40:13,085 --> 00:40:15,955
I really could've settled anywhere.

932
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:17,223
But...

933
00:40:17,223 --> 00:40:18,090
You've already opened one.

934
00:40:18,090 --> 00:40:19,792
I've only been open...

935
00:40:21,060 --> 00:40:24,030
for six or seven months.

936
00:40:24,030 --> 00:40:27,099
So I realized this might be too difficult.

937
00:40:29,602 --> 00:40:33,272
Until I spoke to you just now,

938
00:40:33,272 --> 00:40:36,042
I kept thinking,
"I can be the one to make it work."

939
00:40:36,042 --> 00:40:40,680
I realize now that was one-sided.

940
00:40:40,680 --> 00:40:42,848
But after talking with you,

941
00:40:43,516 --> 00:40:44,884
I realized our circumstances...

942
00:40:45,918 --> 00:40:50,223
could make things very difficult...

943
00:40:50,223 --> 00:40:51,157
for both of us.

944
00:40:51,924 --> 00:40:53,659
That's what I began to think.

945
00:40:58,097 --> 00:40:59,632
So we should end this here.

946
00:41:01,033 --> 00:41:02,768
So we should end this here.

947
00:41:02,768 --> 00:41:03,736
No.

948
00:41:06,539 --> 00:41:07,940
- Yes.
- That's right.

949
00:41:08,975 --> 00:41:10,343
Find another path.

950
00:41:10,343 --> 00:41:11,744
No, I was rooting for them.

951
00:41:11,744 --> 00:41:15,381
If they leave things vague,

952
00:41:15,381 --> 00:41:17,049
that isn't easy either.

953
00:41:17,049 --> 00:41:18,751
For her sake too,

954
00:41:18,985 --> 00:41:22,755
I thought it would be best...

955
00:41:22,755 --> 00:41:24,357
to be clear and end it there.

956
00:41:25,525 --> 00:41:29,028
Maybe I jumped to conclusions too quickly.

957
00:41:36,536 --> 00:41:39,305
I didn't actually come here
to say goodbye.

958
00:41:43,643 --> 00:41:45,244
So it does leave me disappointed.

959
00:41:47,747 --> 00:41:49,015
The conversation had been so good.

960
00:41:52,251 --> 00:41:53,853
They're suddenly breaking up.

961
00:41:56,188 --> 00:41:58,324
Maybe I should've looked for a solution...

962
00:42:02,662 --> 00:42:05,598
before coming to talk to you.

963
00:42:06,599 --> 00:42:07,833
She clearly still has feelings.

964
00:42:10,503 --> 00:42:13,606
But you're too smart for that, Ha Yoon.

965
00:42:13,606 --> 00:42:14,540
What do you mean?

966
00:42:16,342 --> 00:42:19,145
You probably considered
every possible solution already.

967
00:42:21,981 --> 00:42:23,216
Either way,

968
00:42:25,218 --> 00:42:26,919
I'm rooting for you, Ha Yoon.

969
00:42:26,919 --> 00:42:28,854
Of course. I am too.

970
00:42:29,555 --> 00:42:30,656
Good.

971
00:42:30,656 --> 00:42:32,191
That's how he keeps the door open.

972
00:42:32,692 --> 00:42:34,126
It's better than dragging things out.

973
00:42:34,126 --> 00:42:36,863
Now that he's said that, Ha Yoon is...

974
00:42:36,863 --> 00:42:38,164
She's wavering.

975
00:42:38,164 --> 00:42:39,031
She's wavering.

976
00:42:39,031 --> 00:42:42,101
"Should I have thought it through more
before talking to him?"

977
00:42:42,101 --> 00:42:43,970
I always say this.

978
00:42:43,970 --> 00:42:47,506
When a man says,
"I'll be rooting for you," and turns away,

979
00:42:47,506 --> 00:42:50,142
the woman starts wondering,

980
00:42:50,142 --> 00:42:51,477
- "What was that?"
- "What's with him?"

981
00:42:51,477 --> 00:42:53,779
"I thought he only had eyes for me."

982
00:42:53,779 --> 00:42:54,747
(A whole romance drama in seconds)

983
00:42:54,747 --> 00:42:56,115
I like this too.

984
00:42:56,115 --> 00:42:59,051
Then you start thinking,

985
00:42:59,051 --> 00:43:01,587
"Is this really...

986
00:43:01,587 --> 00:43:04,557
a problem we absolutely can't solve?"

987
00:43:04,557 --> 00:43:06,192
But listening to them now,

988
00:43:06,192 --> 00:43:08,861
it's like they dated and broke up.

989
00:43:08,861 --> 00:43:11,364
I actually think...

990
00:43:11,364 --> 00:43:13,599
this is a very good sign.

991
00:43:14,467 --> 00:43:18,404
Honestly, what I wanted to hear was,

992
00:43:18,404 --> 00:43:19,805
"Don't worry about that."

993
00:43:20,506 --> 00:43:21,974
See? I told you.

994
00:43:23,142 --> 00:43:27,380
"Let's set that issue aside
and talk some more."

995
00:43:28,748 --> 00:43:30,950
I think that's what I wanted him to say.

996
00:43:30,950 --> 00:43:32,285
I hadn't known it before,

997
00:43:33,452 --> 00:43:35,388
but I think...

998
00:43:35,388 --> 00:43:37,356
my feelings for him had grown quite a lot.

999
00:43:37,356 --> 00:43:38,824
- Exactly.
- See?

1000
00:43:38,824 --> 00:43:39,992
I told you.

1001
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:41,994
It's because
he cut things off so decisively.

1002
00:43:41,994 --> 00:43:45,932
"I'll be rooting for you" really worked.

1003
00:43:46,465 --> 00:43:49,402
There was no point telling her...

1004
00:43:49,402 --> 00:43:51,938
how many times a month he could visit.

1005
00:43:51,938 --> 00:43:53,472
I'm way too invested in this.

1006
00:43:53,472 --> 00:43:54,874
This couple is driving me crazy.

1007
00:43:55,775 --> 00:43:57,777
Do you know who I met?

1008
00:43:58,778 --> 00:44:00,913
I met Da Hye.

1009
00:44:00,913 --> 00:44:01,881
Okay.

1010
00:44:03,049 --> 00:44:06,118
Da Hye's mother is very outgoing.

1011
00:44:06,118 --> 00:44:10,590
I thought Da Hye and I might click,
so I met her.

1012
00:44:10,590 --> 00:44:11,791
Sure enough,

1013
00:44:12,325 --> 00:44:14,327
Da Hye also...

1014
00:44:14,327 --> 00:44:17,430
has a really grounded outlook.

1015
00:44:21,234 --> 00:44:22,301
Gosh.

1016
00:44:22,902 --> 00:44:27,506
When I asked how she felt
about long-distance relationships,

1017
00:44:27,506 --> 00:44:29,742
she said it might be hard right now,

1018
00:44:29,742 --> 00:44:32,345
but in a few months,

1019
00:44:33,279 --> 00:44:35,481
she thought it could work.

1020
00:44:38,150 --> 00:44:40,086
He's still hung up on her.

1021
00:44:40,086 --> 00:44:42,154
Because he's just gone through a breakup.

1022
00:44:43,322 --> 00:44:45,324
Maybe I shouldn't have met her.

1023
00:44:45,324 --> 00:44:48,227
Still, I needed to talk
to everyone at least once.

1024
00:44:48,227 --> 00:44:51,297
Da Hye is wonderful too.
Everyone here is so nice.

1025
00:44:52,965 --> 00:44:54,433
Well...

1026
00:44:57,436 --> 00:44:59,639
(Glance)

1027
00:45:02,174 --> 00:45:05,111
You seem determined
to keep pursuing Ha Yoon.

1028
00:45:06,812 --> 00:45:08,314
Well...

1029
00:45:09,382 --> 00:45:11,684
Think about it and tell me later.

1030
00:45:12,718 --> 00:45:15,087
Distance is the biggest problem
for everyone.

1031
00:45:15,087 --> 00:45:15,888
Right.

1032
00:45:15,888 --> 00:45:16,889
It's a dilemma.

1033
00:45:18,491 --> 00:45:20,526
Is long distance
really such a big problem?

1034
00:45:21,661 --> 00:45:23,663
Are you okay with it?

1035
00:45:23,663 --> 00:45:24,964
For me,

1036
00:45:25,932 --> 00:45:29,535
I don't mind as long as
I'm the one doing the traveling.

1037
00:45:29,535 --> 00:45:31,003
That's what you think?

1038
00:45:31,003 --> 00:45:35,174
But you can't put that burden on her.

1039
00:45:35,508 --> 00:45:37,910
It isn't about burdening her.

1040
00:45:37,910 --> 00:45:41,514
If you visit once, she'd come once too.

1041
00:45:41,514 --> 00:45:42,682
There's that too.

1042
00:45:43,416 --> 00:45:45,885
She'd have to take time away from work.

1043
00:45:47,119 --> 00:45:49,155
Everyone here is ambitious
about their careers.

1044
00:45:50,623 --> 00:45:51,991
All right.

1045
00:45:53,392 --> 00:45:56,495
That's why you shouldn't be too greedy.

1046
00:45:58,798 --> 00:46:01,334
Just forget it.

1047
00:46:03,169 --> 00:46:05,638
He's only known her for a few days.

1048
00:46:05,638 --> 00:46:06,939
You can move on.

1049
00:46:07,840 --> 00:46:10,776
- Don't give up.
- It isn't that serious yet.

1050
00:46:10,776 --> 00:46:15,514
Think of it as a chance
to meet someone even better.

1051
00:46:25,157 --> 00:46:26,392
Hello.

1052
00:46:26,392 --> 00:46:28,361
(The contestants gather
at the restaurant for dinner.)

1053
00:46:28,361 --> 00:46:29,595
Can you get around okay now?

1054
00:46:30,563 --> 00:46:33,065
Ha Yoon helped me out.

1055
00:46:34,300 --> 00:46:35,968
- I have my socks.
- I'm fine.

1056
00:46:35,968 --> 00:46:36,769
(Hands them over)

1057
00:46:36,769 --> 00:46:38,738
- Thank you.
- Why did you get here so late?

1058
00:46:38,738 --> 00:46:40,139
I know. Sorry I'm late.

1059
00:46:40,139 --> 00:46:41,140
It's fine.

1060
00:46:41,607 --> 00:46:42,608
It's Andong-style braised chicken.

1061
00:46:42,608 --> 00:46:45,645
(Tonight's dinner is
Andong-style braised chicken.)

1062
00:46:49,715 --> 00:46:50,850
The heartbroken man.

1063
00:46:58,391 --> 00:47:00,960
(Hesitating)

1064
00:47:00,960 --> 00:47:02,094
Are the seats assigned?

1065
00:47:02,094 --> 00:47:02,929
No.

1066
00:47:02,929 --> 00:47:04,363
Sit wherever you're comfortable.

1067
00:47:05,331 --> 00:47:08,267
Did you deliberately
leave space between yourselves?

1068
00:47:08,267 --> 00:47:10,703
We wanted to see where you'd sit.

1069
00:47:10,703 --> 00:47:13,406
You wanted to see where we'd sit?

1070
00:47:13,406 --> 00:47:15,474
We wanted to see where you'd sit.

1071
00:47:15,942 --> 00:47:18,344
I wish they'd just relax
around each other.

1072
00:47:20,146 --> 00:47:23,282
(He chooses the seat beside Da Hye.)

1073
00:47:23,282 --> 00:47:24,183
Good work.

1074
00:47:24,183 --> 00:47:25,718
- Did you make all this yourselves?
- Yes.

1075
00:47:29,488 --> 00:47:33,759
It turns out I'm the only one
from outside the capital region.

1076
00:47:33,759 --> 00:47:34,660
You're right.

1077
00:47:34,660 --> 00:47:35,695
I feel very lonely.

1078
00:47:37,230 --> 00:47:38,164
Do you?

1079
00:47:39,131 --> 00:47:40,366
This feels like a dating show.

1080
00:47:40,366 --> 00:47:41,767
That'll make her even more self-conscious.

1081
00:47:41,767 --> 00:47:43,936
You're right.
It really does feel like a dating show.

1082
00:47:43,936 --> 00:47:46,439
(Match to Marry is,
in fact, a dating show.)

1083
00:47:46,439 --> 00:47:47,907
Isn't it kind of like lemonade?

1084
00:47:47,907 --> 00:47:49,242
Right. Something tart.

1085
00:47:49,242 --> 00:47:50,776
Dip it in the sauce.

1086
00:47:50,776 --> 00:47:51,844
Sorry? Okay.

1087
00:47:52,445 --> 00:47:53,412
Thank you.

1088
00:47:53,412 --> 00:47:54,480
You like the sauce.

1089
00:47:54,881 --> 00:47:56,949
I heard you watched the mothers' game.

1090
00:47:56,949 --> 00:47:58,651
I heard my mom worked really hard.

1091
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:02,421
And because her legs are so long,

1092
00:48:02,421 --> 00:48:03,723
she barely needed to take any steps.

1093
00:48:06,058 --> 00:48:08,394
I heard Ye Chan's mother was incredible...

1094
00:48:09,562 --> 00:48:10,897
with the hula hoop.

1095
00:48:10,897 --> 00:48:12,732
I think she learned belly dancing
just for today.

1096
00:48:12,732 --> 00:48:13,766
She was incredible.

1097
00:48:15,535 --> 00:48:16,402
Incredible.

1098
00:48:16,802 --> 00:48:19,038
All the mothers went out.

1099
00:48:21,007 --> 00:48:22,608
So they have the place to themselves.

1100
00:48:22,875 --> 00:48:25,278
(A little earlier)

1101
00:48:25,778 --> 00:48:28,814
(Rustling around)

1102
00:48:29,282 --> 00:48:32,885
(The mothers hurriedly pack their bags.)

1103
00:48:32,885 --> 00:48:33,819
My gosh.

1104
00:48:35,454 --> 00:48:36,389
Let's go together.

1105
00:48:38,624 --> 00:48:40,693
(While their children are eating,)

1106
00:48:40,693 --> 00:48:41,627
(they secretly carry out the plan.)

1107
00:48:41,627 --> 00:48:42,762
They need time like that.

1108
00:48:43,396 --> 00:48:45,765
- I just threw everything in.
- So did I.

1109
00:48:45,765 --> 00:48:47,967
Are we sneaking out
in the middle of the night?

1110
00:48:47,967 --> 00:48:49,302
We're making a run for it.

1111
00:48:49,302 --> 00:48:50,303
Let's go.

1112
00:48:50,536 --> 00:48:52,371
What is this, a 007 mission?

1113
00:48:52,371 --> 00:48:54,073
We're suddenly running away from home.

1114
00:48:54,073 --> 00:48:55,608
I've never done this, so I had no idea.

1115
00:48:55,608 --> 00:48:56,609
(The mothers briefly leave
for their children's sake.)

1116
00:48:56,609 --> 00:48:58,644
The mothers must have been
so excited then.

1117
00:48:58,644 --> 00:49:00,012
Exactly.

1118
00:49:00,012 --> 00:49:01,480
They could do some sightseeing too.

1119
00:49:01,480 --> 00:49:02,982
It was wonderful.

1120
00:49:03,950 --> 00:49:06,018
When I heard they'd be out tonight,

1121
00:49:06,018 --> 00:49:07,320
I was excited...

1122
00:49:07,853 --> 00:49:10,423
that we'd be able to talk more freely.

1123
00:49:10,423 --> 00:49:13,459
I'd get to talk more with the men tonight.

1124
00:49:13,860 --> 00:49:16,996
(What will happen
with only the contestants left tonight?)

1125
00:49:16,996 --> 00:49:19,065
What's that?

1126
00:49:19,065 --> 00:49:22,869
I heard it's great to take
before you drink.

1127
00:49:22,869 --> 00:49:24,871
I've tried it before too.

1128
00:49:24,871 --> 00:49:26,739
- The powder dissolves really well.
- It does.

1129
00:49:26,739 --> 00:49:28,174
You'll have to finish all of it.

1130
00:49:29,876 --> 00:49:30,776
It's good, right?

1131
00:49:30,776 --> 00:49:31,911
- It is.
- Really?

1132
00:49:31,911 --> 00:49:33,145
It is. Try some.

1133
00:49:34,013 --> 00:49:36,716
It tastes like a sports drink,
so it goes down easily.

1134
00:49:37,717 --> 00:49:38,651
It's good.

1135
00:49:40,119 --> 00:49:41,888
How about a truth game with Jenga?

1136
00:49:43,022 --> 00:49:44,123
That sounds good.

1137
00:49:44,496 --> 00:49:47,265
- Like the truth games we played as kids.
- A truth game.

1138
00:49:47,265 --> 00:49:48,934
Are the penalties written on the blocks?

1139
00:49:48,934 --> 00:49:50,268
They have questions.

1140
00:49:50,268 --> 00:49:51,803
I'll peek at one.

1141
00:49:54,673 --> 00:49:55,807
Why are you looking alone?

1142
00:49:55,807 --> 00:49:57,075
We should all look.

1143
00:49:57,609 --> 00:50:00,245
"A physical trait of the person
you're most curious about?"

1144
00:50:00,245 --> 00:50:01,913
I guess they're questions like this.

1145
00:50:01,913 --> 00:50:02,714
This will be fun.

1146
00:50:02,714 --> 00:50:04,249
You suggested it, so you start.

1147
00:50:04,749 --> 00:50:06,618
- You go first.
- You're already in the perfect spot.

1148
00:50:06,618 --> 00:50:08,586
Being first is nice.
There are plenty to choose from.

1149
00:50:08,586 --> 00:50:09,654
(Seong Mo goes first.)

1150
00:50:11,456 --> 00:50:12,424
Read it.

1151
00:50:12,424 --> 00:50:15,660
"Choose your top picks
for looks and personality."

1152
00:50:16,194 --> 00:50:17,729
That's a tough one.

1153
00:50:17,729 --> 00:50:19,297
That really is tough.

1154
00:50:20,765 --> 00:50:22,567
Top pick for looks
and top pick for personality?

1155
00:50:22,567 --> 00:50:23,735
That's hard.

1156
00:50:24,169 --> 00:50:26,938
The person he really likes here...

1157
00:50:26,938 --> 00:50:29,274
- is the top pick for looks.
- That's the way to go.

1158
00:50:29,274 --> 00:50:30,942
Top pick for personality...

1159
00:50:30,942 --> 00:50:32,544
is not a good thing at all.

1160
00:50:32,544 --> 00:50:33,945
That's the worst.

1161
00:50:33,945 --> 00:50:35,246
Looks...

1162
00:50:36,748 --> 00:50:38,049
What do I do?

1163
00:50:39,951 --> 00:50:42,587
Kang Hyeon is my top pick for personality.

1164
00:50:44,689 --> 00:50:45,857
My goodness.

1165
00:50:45,857 --> 00:50:47,058
What now?

1166
00:50:47,058 --> 00:50:49,694
I said something stupid earlier.

1167
00:50:49,694 --> 00:50:51,363
I take back what I said.

1168
00:50:51,363 --> 00:50:52,464
Poor her.

1169
00:50:52,464 --> 00:50:55,100
I'm sorry, Kang Hyeon.

1170
00:50:56,601 --> 00:50:59,037
Kang Hyeon is my top pick for personality.

1171
00:51:00,905 --> 00:51:03,008
Kang Hyeon was wonderful
with the adults from the start.

1172
00:51:03,008 --> 00:51:03,808
Absolutely.

1173
00:51:04,376 --> 00:51:06,544
(Number one in looks)

1174
00:51:06,544 --> 00:51:07,479
Jeong Yoon.

1175
00:51:08,647 --> 00:51:09,581
Thank you.

1176
00:51:11,483 --> 00:51:13,285
That means she's his type.

1177
00:51:13,285 --> 00:51:14,352
Right.

1178
00:51:14,352 --> 00:51:17,222
She's the one he likes most.

1179
00:51:18,757 --> 00:51:21,259
We're giving her a hand.
You're in first place.

1180
00:51:21,259 --> 00:51:23,495
- You have to put it on top.
- I do?

1181
00:51:24,429 --> 00:51:26,097
- My turn.
- Your turn.

1182
00:51:26,097 --> 00:51:28,333
(In Kwon goes next.)

1183
00:51:30,835 --> 00:51:31,670
Safe.

1184
00:51:32,304 --> 00:51:34,673
"Name three things you like
about your top choice."

1185
00:51:35,440 --> 00:51:38,176
- That's manageable.
- "Without naming her."

1186
00:51:40,412 --> 00:51:41,613
First, she's pretty.

1187
00:51:43,014 --> 00:51:44,015
Second,

1188
00:51:46,551 --> 00:51:48,386
when we talk,

1189
00:51:48,386 --> 00:51:50,722
she holds eye contact really well.

1190
00:51:51,690 --> 00:51:52,891
And third,

1191
00:51:54,926 --> 00:51:56,695
I really like her mother.

1192
00:51:56,695 --> 00:51:58,697
She's my favorite mother.

1193
00:51:59,998 --> 00:52:01,766
Okay.

1194
00:52:03,168 --> 00:52:06,137
Those are all traits of Jeong Yoon,
who's number one on my list.

1195
00:52:06,871 --> 00:52:11,042
I wanted her to think,

1196
00:52:11,042 --> 00:52:12,677
"Could he mean me?"

1197
00:52:13,445 --> 00:52:15,380
So I chose my answer carefully.

1198
00:52:16,314 --> 00:52:17,215
Let's go.

1199
00:52:17,215 --> 00:52:19,751
(Next is Jeong Yoon's turn.)

1200
00:52:20,785 --> 00:52:22,554
This one came up again.

1201
00:52:22,921 --> 00:52:24,356
You picked that one.

1202
00:52:25,557 --> 00:52:27,058
"A physical trait, fair skin."

1203
00:52:27,626 --> 00:52:28,893
Fair skin?

1204
00:52:28,893 --> 00:52:30,495
That's so vague.

1205
00:52:30,495 --> 00:52:31,262
Fair skin?

1206
00:52:31,262 --> 00:52:32,864
Who's the fairest person there?

1207
00:52:32,864 --> 00:52:33,765
Fair skin?

1208
00:52:33,765 --> 00:52:36,835
I think she feels the same way I do,

1209
00:52:36,835 --> 00:52:38,637
so I believe she meant me.

1210
00:52:38,637 --> 00:52:42,207
Announcer Lee In Kwon is fair-skinned,

1211
00:52:42,207 --> 00:52:44,376
- and so is...
- He's fair too.

1212
00:52:44,376 --> 00:52:45,477
Ye Chan.

1213
00:52:45,477 --> 00:52:47,512
When she said "fair skin,"

1214
00:52:47,512 --> 00:52:49,314
I started wondering whether she meant me,

1215
00:52:49,314 --> 00:52:52,117
and I wanted to talk to her more.
I felt drawn to her.

1216
00:52:52,117 --> 00:52:53,818
That's what went through my mind.

1217
00:52:54,452 --> 00:52:55,587
Fair skin?

1218
00:52:55,587 --> 00:52:56,821
The person you're curious about?

1219
00:52:56,821 --> 00:52:58,256
He has fair skin.

1220
00:52:58,990 --> 00:53:01,626
Jeong Yoon is the most popular right now.

1221
00:53:01,626 --> 00:53:02,594
You're right.

1222
00:53:02,594 --> 00:53:06,765
Apart from Shin Woo and Dong Young,
the other three...

1223
00:53:06,765 --> 00:53:09,668
seem to be competing for Jeong Yoon.

1224
00:53:09,668 --> 00:53:11,002
- It does look that way.
- They keep coming.

1225
00:53:11,836 --> 00:53:13,638
(Da Hye goes next.)

1226
00:53:13,638 --> 00:53:15,573
That's hard to do.

1227
00:53:17,409 --> 00:53:18,310
That's impressive.

1228
00:53:18,310 --> 00:53:19,945
Did you shake it like that
on purpose before pulling it?

1229
00:53:19,945 --> 00:53:23,415
"Could the person you like change?"

1230
00:53:25,951 --> 00:53:27,018
That's an easy one.

1231
00:53:27,285 --> 00:53:29,087
- Yes.
- Just hypothetically.

1232
00:53:29,087 --> 00:53:30,388
Yes.

1233
00:53:30,388 --> 00:53:32,757
- She might change her mind?
- Yes.

1234
00:53:35,026 --> 00:53:37,495
Suddenly, I'm feeling...

1235
00:53:37,495 --> 00:53:38,897
a bit unsettled.

1236
00:53:39,831 --> 00:53:42,534
I'm getting anxious wondering...

1237
00:53:42,534 --> 00:53:44,903
who might sway Da Hye.

1238
00:53:45,804 --> 00:53:47,272
He must assume he's her favorite.

1239
00:53:47,272 --> 00:53:50,208
She's headed into a whole new world...

1240
00:53:50,208 --> 00:53:52,410
already.

1241
00:53:53,645 --> 00:53:55,647
- What do I do?
- Now...

1242
00:53:55,647 --> 00:53:56,982
Surely it won't get this far.

1243
00:53:58,783 --> 00:53:59,884
That works?

1244
00:53:59,884 --> 00:54:01,152
That actually works?

1245
00:54:01,152 --> 00:54:02,087
I'm so nervous.

1246
00:54:02,954 --> 00:54:05,924
"Choose your top picks
for looks and personality."

1247
00:54:07,392 --> 00:54:08,526
That's the one I got earlier.

1248
00:54:08,526 --> 00:54:09,995
Right. It's back again.

1249
00:54:13,064 --> 00:54:14,766
Well...

1250
00:54:16,234 --> 00:54:17,569
This is making me think.

1251
00:54:21,673 --> 00:54:22,507
Seriously.

1252
00:54:22,507 --> 00:54:24,009
For looks, Ye Chan.

1253
00:54:27,345 --> 00:54:28,580
For personality...

1254
00:54:30,048 --> 00:54:32,250
- Personality.
- Dong Young?

1255
00:54:32,250 --> 00:54:33,351
In Kwon.

1256
00:54:38,657 --> 00:54:39,791
Lingtea tastes good.

1257
00:54:41,026 --> 00:54:42,794
Lingtea tastes good.

1258
00:54:42,794 --> 00:54:43,995
Stop it.

1259
00:54:44,562 --> 00:54:45,497
(Laughter)

1260
00:54:45,497 --> 00:54:47,899
And there it is, "Lingtea tastes good."

1261
00:54:47,899 --> 00:54:49,901
He said Lingtea tastes good.

1262
00:54:50,602 --> 00:54:52,137
The thing is...

1263
00:54:52,137 --> 00:54:55,774
Earlier, it was cool when he said,
"I'll be rooting for you."

1264
00:54:55,774 --> 00:54:58,877
He should turn away completely...

1265
00:54:58,877 --> 00:55:01,546
without showing a hint of emotion.

1266
00:55:01,546 --> 00:55:03,915
But now he's rambling...

1267
00:55:03,915 --> 00:55:05,684
and looking hopeful.

1268
00:55:05,684 --> 00:55:06,985
His lingering feelings
are written all over his face.

1269
00:55:06,985 --> 00:55:08,553
Showing that much lingering attachment...

1270
00:55:10,221 --> 00:55:11,890
actually costs him points.

1271
00:55:17,662 --> 00:55:19,598
I hadn't completely stopped caring,

1272
00:55:21,466 --> 00:55:22,434
but gradually,

1273
00:55:23,368 --> 00:55:26,438
I was trying to care less.

1274
00:55:28,106 --> 00:55:32,344
(They are returning to their lodgings
after the game.)

1275
00:55:34,045 --> 00:55:36,648
(Stops)

1276
00:55:37,082 --> 00:55:39,651
How are you now?
Did you get some rest earlier?

1277
00:55:40,518 --> 00:55:41,620
Good work today.

1278
00:55:41,620 --> 00:55:42,754
Good work today.

1279
00:55:42,754 --> 00:55:43,822
Just go inside.

1280
00:55:45,724 --> 00:55:47,359
Go without looking back.

1281
00:55:48,326 --> 00:55:49,828
No!

1282
00:55:49,828 --> 00:55:51,863
- Don't look.
- He's so obviously still hung up on her.

1283
00:55:51,863 --> 00:55:52,697
He must still care.

1284
00:55:52,697 --> 00:55:54,866
Don't look, Dong Young. Just go.

1285
00:55:55,567 --> 00:55:57,168
(Exasperated)

1286
00:55:57,168 --> 00:56:00,171
Why does he keep doing this
after acting so cool?

1287
00:56:01,406 --> 00:56:02,574
Gosh.

1288
00:56:05,677 --> 00:56:08,013
Is there somewhere we can talk?

1289
00:56:08,013 --> 00:56:09,080
Yes, there's a spot inside.

1290
00:56:09,080 --> 00:56:10,215
Really?

1291
00:56:13,018 --> 00:56:14,052
Actually,

1292
00:56:14,753 --> 00:56:16,921
after the three-on-one date,

1293
00:56:16,921 --> 00:56:19,958
Ye Chan said
there were three women he liked.

1294
00:56:19,958 --> 00:56:21,293
I should find out today.

1295
00:56:23,428 --> 00:56:25,363
I've been a little curious about this.

1296
00:56:25,363 --> 00:56:28,767
Among your top three,

1297
00:56:28,767 --> 00:56:30,268
am I one of them?

1298
00:56:30,268 --> 00:56:32,837
Because if I'm not,

1299
00:56:32,837 --> 00:56:35,640
three out of five
isn't exactly a high bar.

1300
00:56:37,042 --> 00:56:38,944
That's true.

1301
00:56:38,944 --> 00:56:40,645
But if...

1302
00:56:40,912 --> 00:56:43,949
I'm not one of your top three,

1303
00:56:43,949 --> 00:56:46,751
and I keep asking you...

1304
00:56:46,751 --> 00:56:48,320
to spend time with me,

1305
00:56:48,320 --> 00:56:50,021
since you need to choose
among those three,

1306
00:56:50,021 --> 00:56:51,890
I thought it could make you
feel a little pressured.

1307
00:56:51,890 --> 00:56:54,359
So I wanted to ask you.

1308
00:56:58,930 --> 00:57:02,701
I'll take the question at face value
and answer it.

1309
00:57:02,701 --> 00:57:04,202
I'll think he'll answer honestly.

1310
00:57:04,202 --> 00:57:05,904
Honestly, you're not one of the three.

1311
00:57:05,904 --> 00:57:07,238
See?

1312
00:57:07,238 --> 00:57:09,474
He's brutally honest.

1313
00:57:11,610 --> 00:57:13,011
You weren't uncomfortable with me?

1314
00:57:13,511 --> 00:57:15,046
No, I wasn't.

1315
00:57:17,015 --> 00:57:18,550
Why are you apologizing to me?

1316
00:57:18,550 --> 00:57:19,751
It's okay.

1317
00:57:20,685 --> 00:57:21,620
I just...

1318
00:57:24,155 --> 00:57:26,191
I don't like ending things.

1319
00:57:27,092 --> 00:57:31,997
I want to meet someone...

1320
00:57:31,997 --> 00:57:34,833
with no real-world obstacles between us.

1321
00:57:34,833 --> 00:57:35,700
And...

1322
00:57:35,700 --> 00:57:37,869
today, I broke up with someone
I'd never even dated.

1323
00:57:39,070 --> 00:57:40,672
- Today?
- Yes.

1324
00:57:42,374 --> 00:57:48,446
After that,
I realized I needed to be much clearer.

1325
00:57:48,446 --> 00:57:49,648
That's how I felt.

1326
00:57:50,482 --> 00:57:52,817
So I wanted to ask you.

1327
00:57:54,252 --> 00:57:57,055
He likes three out of the five women,

1328
00:57:57,055 --> 00:57:58,390
and if I'm not among them,

1329
00:57:58,390 --> 00:58:03,128
I thought it was time to move on.

1330
00:58:03,962 --> 00:58:06,831
(After Ha Yoon leaves,
Ye Chan reviews his list of contestants.)

1331
00:58:07,899 --> 00:58:09,768
Hello.

1332
00:58:09,768 --> 00:58:11,336
Can we talk for a minute?

1333
00:58:11,803 --> 00:58:12,737
(Ye Chan's second visitor is Do Yoon.)

1334
00:58:12,737 --> 00:58:14,072
Do Yoon.

1335
00:58:14,072 --> 00:58:16,174
Do Yoon keeps...

1336
00:58:16,174 --> 00:58:17,909
knocking on Ye Chan's door.

1337
00:58:17,909 --> 00:58:18,977
Yes.

1338
00:58:19,210 --> 00:58:21,179
Can I catch my breath first?

1339
00:58:21,179 --> 00:58:24,382
Such an honored guest
in such humble quarters.

1340
00:58:24,382 --> 00:58:25,350
Thank you.

1341
00:58:26,117 --> 00:58:28,086
Let me tell you what's happened so far.

1342
00:58:28,086 --> 00:58:29,387
What? Did something happen?

1343
00:58:31,122 --> 00:58:35,160
I said earlier that I was interested...

1344
00:58:35,160 --> 00:58:37,429
in three women.

1345
00:58:39,030 --> 00:58:40,332
Those three...

1346
00:58:41,600 --> 00:58:43,935
are Jeong Yoon, Da Hye, and you.

1347
00:58:44,269 --> 00:58:45,537
You're really honest.

1348
00:58:45,537 --> 00:58:47,272
Still, thanks. I'm one of them.

1349
00:58:47,973 --> 00:58:50,842
From day three,
I wanted to focus on those three.

1350
00:58:52,077 --> 00:58:54,779
When we talked one-on-one,

1351
00:58:54,779 --> 00:58:57,115
I thought we really clicked.

1352
00:58:57,115 --> 00:58:58,583
That was last night.

1353
00:58:59,651 --> 00:59:01,319
I really wanted
a one-on-one conversation with you.

1354
00:59:01,319 --> 00:59:04,155
(They went on a date
after Ye Chan chose her last night.)

1355
00:59:04,155 --> 00:59:07,425
Now that it's all out there,
I wanted to talk.

1356
00:59:08,226 --> 00:59:09,294
That's why I came.

1357
00:59:10,829 --> 00:59:11,930
Good. I'm glad you did.

1358
00:59:13,064 --> 00:59:14,065
Right.

1359
00:59:15,066 --> 00:59:18,436
I think those two make a good match too.

1360
00:59:18,436 --> 00:59:22,674
Do Yoon's mother chose him
for her private conversation.

1361
00:59:22,674 --> 00:59:25,610
And Ye Chan grew
more interested in Do Yoon.

1362
00:59:25,610 --> 00:59:27,345
Right, thanks to her mother.

1363
00:59:27,679 --> 00:59:29,347
Wait, my mom...

1364
00:59:29,347 --> 00:59:31,950
You talked to your mother, right?

1365
00:59:31,950 --> 00:59:34,386
She said she picked you.

1366
00:59:34,386 --> 00:59:38,423
After talking with your mother
one-on-one today,

1367
00:59:38,423 --> 00:59:41,226
the practical points she raised...

1368
00:59:42,227 --> 00:59:43,595
made sense to me.

1369
00:59:43,595 --> 00:59:44,629
Right.

1370
00:59:44,629 --> 00:59:48,533
Whether one person
starts a business or something,

1371
00:59:48,533 --> 00:59:54,506
having the other person earn
a steady income...

1372
00:59:54,506 --> 00:59:56,141
- may actually be better.
- It's a good combination.

1373
00:59:56,141 --> 00:59:59,010
I thought that was
a very reasonable point.

1374
00:59:59,010 --> 01:00:01,313
- Right.
- Exactly.

1375
01:00:01,313 --> 01:00:04,049
And my mom chose you as her first choice.

1376
01:00:04,049 --> 01:00:05,984
That's a big factor too.

1377
01:00:05,984 --> 01:00:08,753
And I do like you too.

1378
01:00:08,753 --> 01:00:10,789
That's why I want to keep talking.

1379
01:00:12,490 --> 01:00:13,992
(Stares)

1380
01:00:13,992 --> 01:00:16,361
Why are you staring? You're making me shy.

1381
01:00:16,361 --> 01:00:18,830
Why are you staring so intently?

1382
01:00:20,565 --> 01:00:22,100
- Ye Chan?
- Yes?

1383
01:00:22,100 --> 01:00:23,368
- Are you in there?
- Yes.

1384
01:00:23,368 --> 01:00:24,302
Are you alone?

1385
01:00:24,748 --> 01:00:26,503
- No, I'm with someone.
- My Goodness.

1386
01:00:26,504 --> 01:00:27,739
Who is it?

1387
01:00:27,739 --> 01:00:30,542
- Who is it?
- He really is the king of the ladies.

1388
01:00:31,182 --> 01:00:32,450
Are you saying I can come?

1389
01:00:32,817 --> 01:00:34,386
You're still talking.
Are you sure I can come?

1390
01:00:34,386 --> 01:00:35,587
It's her.

1391
01:00:36,488 --> 01:00:37,856
She...

1392
01:00:37,856 --> 01:00:39,724
never disappoints us.

1393
01:00:40,725 --> 01:00:42,160
Do you want to...

1394
01:00:42,160 --> 01:00:43,428
It's okay. I should get going now.

1395
01:00:44,229 --> 01:00:45,730
It's okay. I should get going now.

1396
01:00:45,730 --> 01:00:47,799
No, that's not what I meant.

1397
01:00:47,799 --> 01:00:49,701
We've already talked for a while.

1398
01:00:49,701 --> 01:00:51,703
Come on up.

1399
01:00:51,703 --> 01:00:53,204
I really don't want to steal him away.

1400
01:00:53,204 --> 01:00:55,740
You're not stealing him.
We've talked plenty.

1401
01:00:56,207 --> 01:01:00,445
I'll be quick, then.
You two can set another time.

1402
01:01:00,445 --> 01:01:02,280
We'll figure that out ourselves.

1403
01:01:02,280 --> 01:01:03,715
- See you.
- Sorry.

1404
01:01:03,715 --> 01:01:05,483
But this place...

1405
01:01:05,483 --> 01:01:06,551
is a palace.

1406
01:01:07,886 --> 01:01:09,487
I'll get going.

1407
01:01:11,623 --> 01:01:15,427
We should still talk, right?

1408
01:01:15,427 --> 01:01:18,363
We started feeling each other out earlier,
then stopped.

1409
01:01:19,030 --> 01:01:22,167
How many people
do you still want to talk to?

1410
01:01:22,167 --> 01:01:23,702
I've actually narrowed it down.

1411
01:01:24,202 --> 01:01:25,804
Already?

1412
01:01:25,804 --> 01:01:29,507
Seong Mo and you.

1413
01:01:31,076 --> 01:01:32,110
I see.

1414
01:01:32,410 --> 01:01:34,679
Back at the pavilion,
when I said that to you,

1415
01:01:34,679 --> 01:01:36,948
you chose your words very carefully,

1416
01:01:36,948 --> 01:01:39,150
and I could tell
you were trying not to say too much.

1417
01:01:40,652 --> 01:01:42,654
I kept feeling...

1418
01:01:42,654 --> 01:01:44,823
like I was the only one making an effort.

1419
01:01:45,890 --> 01:01:47,959
You realized that now?

1420
01:01:49,461 --> 01:01:53,465
But I wanted to talk today
about our views on faith.

1421
01:01:53,465 --> 01:01:54,866
- Our views on faith.
- Yes.

1422
01:01:56,401 --> 01:01:57,669
Views on faith?

1423
01:01:58,737 --> 01:02:00,205
It's a pretty deep topic.

1424
01:02:04,809 --> 01:02:05,810
This is difficult.

1425
01:02:05,810 --> 01:02:07,145
It is.

1426
01:02:07,145 --> 01:02:09,848
That was a hard question. Sorry.

1427
01:02:09,848 --> 01:02:11,283
That's not what I mean.

1428
01:02:12,117 --> 01:02:13,752
I just don't think I can answer right now.

1429
01:02:13,752 --> 01:02:15,053
It's difficult?

1430
01:02:15,053 --> 01:02:16,087
Knock, knock.

1431
01:02:17,088 --> 01:02:18,890
- Hello.
- Who is it?

1432
01:02:18,890 --> 01:02:21,626
(The fourth visitor already,
Who is it this time?)

1433
01:02:21,626 --> 01:02:22,894
It's Da Hye.

1434
01:02:22,894 --> 01:02:24,195
Come in.

1435
01:02:24,195 --> 01:02:26,298
He really is the king of the ladies.

1436
01:02:26,298 --> 01:02:27,499
Unbelievable.

1437
01:02:28,333 --> 01:02:30,035
How long have you been talking?

1438
01:02:30,035 --> 01:02:31,536
About 15 minutes?

1439
01:02:31,536 --> 01:02:33,438
Then I'll come back later.

1440
01:02:33,438 --> 01:02:35,740
It's fine.

1441
01:02:35,740 --> 01:02:38,877
Talk a little longer.

1442
01:02:38,877 --> 01:02:40,579
Ye Chan, get some exercise later.

1443
01:02:40,579 --> 01:02:42,080
Come down,
then we can walk back up together.

1444
01:02:42,080 --> 01:02:43,949
Okay, let's do that.

1445
01:02:43,949 --> 01:02:44,983
Go on ahead.

1446
01:02:44,983 --> 01:02:46,318
Wait, Kang Hyeon...

1447
01:02:46,318 --> 01:02:48,787
is just staying?

1448
01:02:48,787 --> 01:02:50,121
She isn't giving up her turn?

1449
01:02:50,121 --> 01:02:52,557
Do Yoon gave way when she arrived.

1450
01:02:53,458 --> 01:02:55,293
Why isn't Kang Hyeon doing the same?

1451
01:02:55,293 --> 01:02:57,395
She said they'd already talked
for 15 minutes.

1452
01:02:59,965 --> 01:03:01,866
(Meanwhile, Shin Woo heads somewhere.)

1453
01:03:01,866 --> 01:03:03,702
Shin Woo's here.

1454
01:03:06,771 --> 01:03:07,706
Excuse me.

1455
01:03:07,706 --> 01:03:09,007
Who is he looking for?

1456
01:03:09,007 --> 01:03:10,475
Is Da Hye here?

1457
01:03:10,475 --> 01:03:11,843
- Yes.
- Da Hye.

1458
01:03:12,239 --> 01:03:13,244
Who is it?

1459
01:03:13,245 --> 01:03:14,579
Can you come out for a moment?

1460
01:03:14,579 --> 01:03:16,815
Yes, but...

1461
01:03:16,815 --> 01:03:19,017
I said...

1462
01:03:19,017 --> 01:03:20,819
I'd talk to Ye Chan...

1463
01:03:21,386 --> 01:03:23,455
in about 15 minutes.

1464
01:03:23,455 --> 01:03:24,422
Then,

1465
01:03:24,422 --> 01:03:25,690
could you come find me then?

1466
01:03:25,690 --> 01:03:26,625
Yes, I'll come.

1467
01:03:26,625 --> 01:03:27,659
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

1468
01:03:28,693 --> 01:03:32,297
It would've been better
if Shin Woo had taken tonight off.

1469
01:03:32,297 --> 01:03:33,732
Shin Woo.

1470
01:03:36,835 --> 01:03:39,271
(Shin Woo and Ye Chan cross paths.)

1471
01:03:39,271 --> 01:03:40,538
Where are you going?

1472
01:03:40,538 --> 01:03:41,740
- Sorry?
- Where are you going?

1473
01:03:41,740 --> 01:03:42,807
I'm going down to talk.

1474
01:03:42,807 --> 01:03:43,808
With whom?

1475
01:03:43,808 --> 01:03:44,576
Da Hye.

1476
01:03:44,576 --> 01:03:46,645
Don't go. You can't go.

1477
01:03:46,645 --> 01:03:49,681
I'm sorry. I'm completely drained.

1478
01:03:49,681 --> 01:03:50,448
Go have a good talk.

1479
01:03:50,448 --> 01:03:51,216
Sorry.

1480
01:03:51,216 --> 01:03:52,317
Please let her go soon.

1481
01:03:55,487 --> 01:03:56,488
Are you there?

1482
01:03:57,088 --> 01:03:57,789
Yes.

1483
01:04:00,158 --> 01:04:01,593
Are you done talking?

1484
01:04:01,593 --> 01:04:04,362
Sorry, it's gotten so late.

1485
01:04:05,163 --> 01:04:07,866
- That was a long...
- They talked for a while.

1486
01:04:07,866 --> 01:04:09,467
They must've talked a long time.

1487
01:04:09,467 --> 01:04:11,036
She kept him too long.

1488
01:04:11,836 --> 01:04:13,838
While listening
to your introduction today,

1489
01:04:16,775 --> 01:04:21,479
a lot of what you said matched
with the direction I'd been thinking of.

1490
01:04:21,479 --> 01:04:25,350
That made me want to talk to you again.

1491
01:04:27,485 --> 01:04:29,921
So I went to find you tonight,
even though it was late.

1492
01:04:30,755 --> 01:04:32,691
The direction.

1493
01:04:32,691 --> 01:04:35,994
What exactly caught
your interest about that?

1494
01:04:35,994 --> 01:04:39,130
To be completely honest,

1495
01:04:39,130 --> 01:04:41,099
I came here...

1496
01:04:41,099 --> 01:04:42,534
thinking about faith.

1497
01:04:43,335 --> 01:04:46,004
I wondered if you had too.

1498
01:04:46,004 --> 01:04:47,038
Or did you simply...

1499
01:04:47,038 --> 01:04:48,306
talk more about Christianity...

1500
01:04:48,306 --> 01:04:51,610
because you're Christian
and I'm Christian too?

1501
01:04:53,645 --> 01:04:55,580
So you're asking...

1502
01:04:55,580 --> 01:04:58,416
whether I came here thinking about that?

1503
01:04:58,416 --> 01:04:59,317
Yes.

1504
01:05:00,518 --> 01:05:03,021
Is that hard to answer?

1505
01:05:06,258 --> 01:05:09,494
Honestly, listening to you, I thought...

1506
01:05:10,428 --> 01:05:13,331
I'm sure it's the same for everyone,

1507
01:05:13,331 --> 01:05:16,368
but I keep freezing
whenever religion comes up...

1508
01:05:16,368 --> 01:05:17,969
because the order feels off.

1509
01:05:17,969 --> 01:05:20,405
Unless you met at church,

1510
01:05:20,405 --> 01:05:22,874
you'd usually talk
about everyday things first,

1511
01:05:22,874 --> 01:05:26,144
see if you connect and your plans line up,

1512
01:05:26,144 --> 01:05:29,180
and then move on to deeper topics.

1513
01:05:30,682 --> 01:05:31,816
That's fair.

1514
01:05:32,684 --> 01:05:34,786
What Ye Chan just said is exactly right.

1515
01:05:34,786 --> 01:05:36,154
It is.

1516
01:05:36,154 --> 01:05:38,924
Faith matters, but first,

1517
01:05:38,924 --> 01:05:42,661
you need to see whether you're compatible
before getting into religion.

1518
01:05:42,661 --> 01:05:44,362
- That's more important.
- Exactly.

1519
01:05:44,362 --> 01:05:45,664
Ye Chan is wondering,

1520
01:05:45,664 --> 01:05:50,535
"Should I choose someone
solely because we share a faith?"

1521
01:05:51,303 --> 01:05:53,271
I'm no longer sure...

1522
01:05:53,271 --> 01:05:54,606
whether Da Hye is still my third choice.

1523
01:05:56,041 --> 01:05:58,843
If that were what I preferred,

1524
01:05:58,843 --> 01:06:02,948
it would've been faster
to look for someone at church.

1525
01:06:03,348 --> 01:06:06,351
Today,
you'll go on a meet-the-parents date.

1526
01:06:06,351 --> 01:06:08,386
(A meet-the-parents date begins
without warning.)

1527
01:06:08,386 --> 01:06:09,454
Right away?

1528
01:06:09,621 --> 01:06:12,357
(An unexpected guest arrives
for the date.)

1529
01:06:12,357 --> 01:06:13,258
Dad.

1530
01:06:13,725 --> 01:06:15,360
- The father must be here.
- A father just showed up.

1531
01:06:15,360 --> 01:06:18,330
(The entire family arrives.)

1532
01:06:18,663 --> 01:06:19,598
(Startled)

1533
01:06:19,598 --> 01:06:21,967
Now it feels like a formal meeting
between the families.

1534
01:06:21,967 --> 01:06:23,235
Can you handle alcohol?

1535
01:06:23,235 --> 01:06:25,303
Where do you see yourself in ten years?

1536
01:06:26,304 --> 01:06:27,706
This is terrifying.

1537
01:06:27,706 --> 01:06:29,608
They're walking on thin ice.

1538
01:06:29,608 --> 01:06:32,377
If it doesn't feel right,
it's best to end it quickly.

1539
01:06:32,377 --> 01:06:34,246
What will they do?

1540
01:06:34,246 --> 01:06:36,514
- This is too much.
- I'm so uncomfortable right now.

1541
01:06:36,514 --> 01:06:37,916
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
